{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine","id":70267,"title":"EX3 Solar Medicine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-11T21:00:50-08:00","id":70267,"title":"EX3 Solar Medicine","content":"Any requests?<br /> <br /> Please try not to ask for things that are already in the 2e set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:05:05-08:00","id":70270,"title":"","content":"Actually putting &quot;create new lifeforms&quot; here rather than a separate pseudo-science crafting system could be rather cool, and perhaps less genre breaking than the alternative.<br /> <br /> Also Fertility Charms might be rather in theme for Solars, given the roles of &quot;Solar Heroes&quot; in myth and ancient religions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-12-2014, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:09:27-08:00","id":70273,"title":"","content":"A &quot;I go where I am needed&quot; Charm for wandering healers (could just be awareness of where people ail, rather than anything Sidereal-style fate/narrative bending).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:10:49-08:00","id":70275,"title":"","content":"Some sort of vaccination/preemptive antidote effect to bolster others' immunity to getting sick or poisoned would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:13:40-08:00","id":70276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70275#post70275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Some sort of vaccination/preemptive antidote effect to bolster others' immunity to getting sick or poisoned would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have this only work for granting immunity to a disease the Solar has personally cured a case of before.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that could spring off from a charm that lets a Solar up RESISTANCE to infection in general, but not grant immunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:15:16-08:00","id":70278,"title":"","content":"Is using Medicine as a weapon thematically reserved to Abyssal and Sidereal Charms (the latter assuming they're still in Saturn's purview)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:15:18-08:00","id":70279,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a &quot;Craftsman Needs No Tools,&quot; sort of deal, where the Solar performs surgery complex surgery with his teeth and a bobby-pin.<br /> <br /> For some reason, I am now envisioning a Solar Hawkeye Pierce. <br /> <br /> I also feel that there may be room in 3e Medicine for a &quot;I'm a Doctor!&quot; charm that allows you to easily assume command of a medical emergency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:15:44-08:00","id":70281,"title":"","content":"I've considered wanting a Solar Medicine Charm that inflicts a healing soporific (branching off of Touch of Blissful Release) which not only makes targets tired, but increases their healing rate / makes other Medicine Charms cheaper while they sleep.<br /> <br /> Also a Charm that, using knowledge of medicine, makes wounds inflicted from an attack far more difficult to heal.<br /> <br /> Charms for leading a team of medics would be great too.<br /> <br /> It might overlap with Survival (which I'm fine with honestly) but Charms that identify the healing capabilities of natural products would be awesome. I always like Charms that incorporate the environment of a scene like that.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Oh, that reminds me. 2e had these Charms for healing poison/crippling/sickness, and could do it even if there was no cure. While cool, I found them sorta boring in-game. Just boom, done. It might be cooler if there were Charms that many not perfectly cure a patient instantly and right then, but always told you a way how: a special plant, a secret technique, whatever -- something out there, if put into the supernal hands of a Solar medic, would have the capability to cure what would otherwise be incurable. Better adventure fodder that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:16:40-08:00","id":70283,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the base 2E Solar Charms were woefully lacking in the &quot;help others resist/become immune to certain effects&quot; department, unfortunately. Would love to see that rectified in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:16:44-08:00","id":70284,"title":"","content":"In general, potions and brewing seem more pertinent to Medicine than Craft to me.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see more Medicine charms that enhance their beneficiaries. Rather than merely curing their ails, cure the ails they never knew they had. Fortify their strength with a mixture that seems dubious to those less learned than you. Readjust their chi flow with acupuncture, fortifying their stamina for a time. That sort of thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/347-mobius","name":"Mobius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:17:11-08:00","id":70285,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure 2e doesn't have any &quot;create a medical formula&quot; charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:17:43-08:00","id":70289,"title":"","content":"Anyone watch Kung Fu hustle? Anyone remember the scene where the guy gets so beaten up, almost all his bones are broken? And then the couple fixes him up and he's even stronger than before because all of his chi channels have been opened up?<br /> <br /> I want a Solar charm that allows you to completely wreck a person, and then make them even stronger than before. There's quite a few Wuxia films where the hero gets stronger because they visited a doctor and acupuncture made them better, or they took some crazy herbal pill and survived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:19:02-08:00","id":70290,"title":"","content":"I'd like medicine charms to be broader, and for the charm tree to be shorter, when it comes to the &quot;standard&quot; healing effects (fast healing, healing without equipment, healing keywords, mass healing) The 2e set was kinda bloated, requiring a charm for every single keyword and restoration buff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:19:08-08:00","id":70291,"title":"","content":"More Charms to cover the healing of psychological damage and/or disorders might be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:20:01-08:00","id":70293,"title":"","content":"Hrm. Did 2e have a Medicine Charm for Solars that acted as a hard de-toxification effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:23:14-08:00","id":70296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70276#post70276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have this only work for granting immunity to a disease the Solar has personally cured a case of before.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that could spring off from a charm that lets a Solar up RESISTANCE to infection in general, but not grant immunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant &quot;bolster immunity&quot; as in &quot;boost the immune system.&quot; A Charm to enhance resistance to general infection, then one that grants immunity to a certain disease/poison - even if only temporarily - would be useful, especially when going into areas where a particular disease or poison is common. Scurvy in the West, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:28:40-08:00","id":70303,"title":"","content":"How about medicine charms that can aid in battle? Like discerning an Aquiles heel or even inflicting one on the target. May sound abysalish but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:33:22-08:00","id":70304,"title":"","content":"Medicine can be used to harm as well as heal. While much of the application of that line of thought is more along the lines of Abyssals, I imagine, I don't see torture as being outside the realm of Solar Charm concepts so that might be interesting to explore.<br /> <br /> Something to create or ration/prolong the supply or effects of medical applications would be cool.<br /> <br /> edit: Was there ever anything covering surgery before? That's an idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":77,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","user":"kongurous","date":". 02-12-2014, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:35:05-08:00","id":70305,"title":"","content":"I would like to see Charms that affect the ability to make and store medicines in Medicine. I want a healer to have a reason to prepare a cure for a disease in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:37:39-08:00","id":70306,"title":"","content":"I've always thought it would be cool for Medicine to some pressure-point style Charm(s) for messing people up - blindness, penalties, temporarily crippling a limb, that sort of thing - using their understanding of the body and the meridians.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I have a long-standing dream to play a kung fu doctor who both attacks and heals people using thrown needles and acupuncture. Now, clearly, custom Thrown Charms would be part of that, but some Medicine Charm that lets you ignore penalties for improvised equipment might also be needed.<br /> <br /> Chinese stories often seem to have expert doctors be able to tell all kinds of things about a person based on the disposition of elements as reflected in breath and so on. Broader information-gathering Medicine Charms sound cool to me.<br /> <br /> More prosaically, it would certainly be useful to have a Medicine Charm which let you create tonics or elixirs which stuck around, even if they were less effective than what you did on your own, so that your allies and servants could have access to it while you're not around.<br /> <br /> And though the potential for abuse must be watched, I have always liked the idea of using Medicine to clear out the chi of people (mortals or Exalts) to help make them more powerful, or better able to focus on a given task.<br /> <br /> Of course, looking at that list... I don't know if any of that is Medicine. It might just be Martial Arts, Thrown, Investigation, Craft, and... lots of skills (War and Lore did it in 2E) respectively. Medicine Charms are tough!<br /> <br /> Arcanus' idea of pre-emptive medice seems really hard to argue, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:42:04-08:00","id":70307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70306#post70306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcanus' idea of pre-emptive medice seems really hard to argue, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dibs on creating a Dragon-Blooded Jenny McCarthy who claims that Anathema Medicine Charms cause demon possession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:44:44-08:00","id":70310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine#post70267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any requests?<br /> <br /> Please try not to ask for things that are already in the 2e set.</div> </div> </div> </div>A system for diseases that integrates well into both the general medical rules and the solar medicine charmset was the main thing I thought 2e's Solar Medicine tree was missing. It was one of the few non-combat trees that felt like it synergized with itself pretty well, since you could combo everything together into a &quot;Lay on Hands&quot; instant healing effect. <br /> <br /> As long as poisons, diseases, crippling effects, and gross physical trauma are all things my Solar Doctor can take care of, I have no complaints.<br /> <br /> <br /> ....That said, since you're <i>asking</i>, I'd like to see more inter-ability synergy. Medical charms that, say, give you bonuses to hitting vital organs with your physical attacks, ones that work well with whatever the poison/medicine making Craft charms are, ones that can help out with interrogation techniques in Investigation and Larceny, and so on.<br /> <br /> (For the record, I expect all the other abilities to reciprocate. Combos and Synergy are big parts of the fun in CCGs and Exalted's charm system is designed much like one of them. Setting things up such that being good at, say, any of the Twilight abilities helps you out with the other four seems like a good way to make a twilight feel more like a twilight, as opposed to a dude who just happens to be good at the thinky stuff.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:51:20-08:00","id":70316,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, once you get to the point where you can rapidly and reliably heal self, heal target and mass heal target, it's hard to think of effects that could be put in medicine. Skyrim had a lot of things that let you put the hurt on undead using raw life force, but that's more a Sidereal thing than Solar. Even A Hood on Death felt extremely weird to me as a Solar charm, despite how cool it is.<br /> <br /> I'm sort of at a loss, beyond inter-ability synergy, I cant think of much else for Solar Medicine to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:56:11-08:00","id":70318,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a charm that allows you to commit motes and give someone bonus dice to prevent their disease--or appropriate condition--from getting worse, allowing the patient to survive just a little while longer:<br /> <br /> Hold on! The doctor is on his way!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:58:06-08:00","id":70319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70318#post70318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see a charm that allows you to commit motes and give someone bonus dice to prevent their disease--or appropriate condition--from getting worse, allowing the patient to survive just a little while longer:<br /> <br /> Hold on! The doctor is on his way!</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected. That is a brilliant idea and very in-theme for Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:58:34-08:00","id":70320,"title":"","content":"That's why, like the anti-lying Charm from 2E Investigation, it needs to be broken down a bit. The base 2E Solar Charms pretty much run the gamut, minus a few areas (vaccination, psychological treatment, physical enhancements, actual medical supplies, etc.). Certain reorganization may be needed as opposed to a straight translation of what's already there. 2E did a good job of avoiding speed bump Charms, but in turn it offered a lot of Charms that - once you had them - made a particular part of the game (being lied to, for instance) not a problem anymore. Luckily, we've got a good team of devs correcting that very problem while adding a lot of new stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:59:19-08:00","id":70321,"title":"","content":"Oh, also! We need a kidney thief charm! In the vein of &quot;Hey, is that a penny behind your ear! Nope, it's your spleen!&quot;. Maybe that's too abyssal, but hey... Thanks for the kidkneez, sucker!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:59:23-08:00","id":70323,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, something not in 2e core.<br /> <br /> I'd like it if the charms worked on both individuals and small groups.<br /> <br /> For example, if the solar comes upon a group of 10 injured soldiers, I'd like it if Wound Mending Care Technique can be used once to treat them instead of once for every soldier who's lost a limb. Likewise, if I go into a village where people have fallen sick with plague, let me cure small groups of villagers at a time with Ailment-Rectifying Method.<br /> <br /> I'd also like a charm that lets me treat the causes of a disease or poison. If the village well has been supernaturally befouled, I'd like a charm that lets me cleanse it.<br /> <br /> If Shadowlands or some of the Creation-altering Blasphemy effects are in 3e, I would like Medicine to be able to 'heal the land' as it were.<br /> <br /> While I can see a martial art centered around medicine, I'd rather not see (solar) medicine charms that cause harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-12-2014, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:02:59-08:00","id":70326,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a charm where a solar can reattach a limb and make it function again.<br /> <br /> Overal though, what I hope happens is that medicine becomes less boring.<br /> A lot of the medicine charms are too universal, so there is nothing interesting you can do with them. Why would I care if someone has a fever or is the first victim of Plaguefather Shen's new disease? The only difference is that I have to roll a few more dice.<br /> Also, because medicine in Exalted can't work like our medicine, due to them essence instead of molecules, I'd like the medical procedures to show that.<br /> Things like the Five Elements in acupuncture, and the way the ancient Greeks explained certain diseases by excesses of different fluids, which are in turn tied to different temperaments.<br /> And I know that in 2e there were diseases of conviction and diseases of Valor, that sort of stuff, but those were really only about the symptoms. Having a disease that's stronger on a person who has a high Valor would make both the disease, and hopefully the way of treating it, much more interesting. It would also explain why some people suffer more from a disease than others.<br /> <br /> I guess what I really want is there to be somewhat of a middleground between the semi-sciency medical things, since those could make actual sense in exalted, and more realistic, surgical procedures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:03:29-08:00","id":70327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70321#post70321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also! We need a kidney thief charm! In the vein of &quot;Hey, is that a penny behind your ear! Nope, it's your spleen!&quot;. Maybe that's too abyssal, but hey... Thanks for the kidkneez, sucker!</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me that an autopsy Charm would be good, although it could just be a specific application of Flawless Diagnosis Technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:04:51-08:00","id":70329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70323#post70323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like a charm that lets me treat the causes of a disease or poison. If the village well has been supernaturally befouled, I'd like a charm that lets me cleanse it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, that is shiny as a high-Essence way to upgrade the basic anti poison and disease Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:06:36-08:00","id":70333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70323#post70323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like a charm that lets me treat the causes of a disease or poison. If the village well has been supernaturally befouled, I'd like a charm that lets me cleanse it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This x 1000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:09:26-08:00","id":70335,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, I could also see the ability to prescribe dietary and/or exercise regimens that provide some sort of bonus effect if they are fulfilled, like resisting or healing Wyld Mutation or training certain traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:09:47-08:00","id":70336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70306#post70306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chinese stories often seem to have expert doctors be able to tell all kinds of things about a person based on the disposition of elements as reflected in breath and so on. Broader information-gathering Medicine Charms sound cool to me.<br /> <br /> More prosaically, it would certainly be useful to have a Medicine Charm which let you create tonics or elixirs which stuck around, even if they were less effective than what you did on your own, so that your allies and servants could have access to it while you're not around.<br /> <br /> And though the potential for abuse must be watched, I have always liked the idea of using Medicine to clear out the chi of people (mortals or Exalts) to help make them more powerful, or better able to focus on a given task.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are really cool ideas that I second. Especially the first: would not have thought about super prognosis and diagnosis Charms beyond the strict realm of physical health. And mental health, if someone else's more psychiatric suggestion works out.<br /> <br /> Chaining the three together, maybe after an investigation, a Solar can proscribe a self-improvement dietary and exercise regime perfectly tailored to the individual: if followed, the patient could get bonuses in training Skills/Attributes, longer-term resistance to disease and other maladies, and other potential bennies long after the doctor has departed.<br /> EDIT: Sidereal'd by Mockery.<br /> <br /> On the topic of psychologically themed Charms, I really do like the notion, and then some. Some doctors heal the body. Others, the mind. And some... heal the heart. Whether an old scar of an Intimacy that still aches, or an imbalance of Virtues ruining one's life, the Lawgiver can help a patient to let go and move on or to better moderate those drives, leading to a happier, healthier life.<br /> <br /> Ah, and medical breakthroughs that other practitioners of Medicine can learn and use themselves without a Solar's presence would also be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 02-12-2014, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:11:03-08:00","id":70337,"title":"","content":"Medicine Charms Ideas<br /> <br /> * The Solar knows exactly how to manipulate the body to unlock it's potential and push it to it's limit. The Solar unleashes a quick succession of hyper accurate finger tip strikes to pressure points. The recipient chooses how many bashing health levels they would like to spend on top of the Exalt's expenditure. These health levels spent can only be healed naturally. For each health level spent, the target adds one die to all Physical and Mental dice pools. This person cannot have this Charm used on them again until they heal all damaged taken by this Charm.<br /> <br /> * Breathing deeply, the Solar takes complete control of their meridians and chakra points in whole. The Solar may spend 1 Willpower to recover X motes, Y bashing damage for Y motes or Z lethal damage for Z motes. This may be done freely on your turn as long as this Charm is active.<br /> <br /> * Staring into his patient's eyes, the Solar forces his brain to sleep and his subconciousness to the surface. Memories forgotten, details missed and unaltered sensory detail can be accessed in this state.<br /> <br /> * Taking hypnotism to the next level, the Solar can project an image into an opponents mind in the heat of combat, without even having to look into the opponents mind. Momentum mechanics here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/132-crescens","name":"Crescens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:12:39-08:00","id":70338,"title":"","content":"Maybe something generally health related? Like a supertonic that provides a list of small effects to the user? I remember all these magical fixes and devices sold on the internet and infomercials, so something like a miraculous supertonic seems right up a Solar's ally.<br /> <br /> It could maybe do stuff like:<br /> <br /> -Remove aging penalties to attributes (grandpa goes from boney weak geezer to ULTRABUFF OLD MAN)<br /> -Remove penalties from sleep deprivation/exhaustion<br /> -Removes pain-based penalties from inherited diseases or old injuries<br /> -Increase stamina for long forced marches<br /> -Provide general resistance to non-life threatening disease like colds or flus<br /> -Allow the digestion of foods normally difficult for human digestion (Plant matter, cheap meats, foods that you are alergic to)<br /> -Provide a natural bloom of health to boost appearance-based rolls by a little<br /> -Lets mortals resist infection and staunch bleeding easier.<br /> -Increases fertility and removes possiblity of inherited diseases/conditions passing onto children.<br /> <br /> It'd be a very mortal-centric charm and need balancing to keep from stepping on other charms/splats toes, but a Miraclous Solar Supertonic isn't too different from tiger warrior training in that regard.<br /> <br /> Maybe each supertonic is unique, like picking from a list of effects when it's brewed? Or purchased as a charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2258-mrstabs","user":"MrStabs","date":". 02-12-2014, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2258-mrstabs","name":"MrStabs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:12:58-08:00","id":70339,"title":"","content":"Let's see, Solar Medicine can:<ul><li>Cure Poison/Crippling/Sickness/Derangement/Mutation.</li> <li>Speed up healing</li> <li>Wound Penalties negator.</li> <li>Converting Aggravated damage into Lethal.</li> <li>Magic diagnosis.</li> <li>Giving people additional HLs.</li> <li>Instant treatment.</li> </ul><br /> Hmmmm, aside from using Medicine to damage opponent , I really can't think of any new effect that are not just some stunt use of those above charms. Maybe charm for diagnosis and banishing mental influence, though I'm not sure if there is such a thing as &quot;Healing Mind-Rape Technique&quot; .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:17:27-08:00","id":70341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70339#post70339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if there is such a thing as &quot;Healing Mind-Rape Technique&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind-Soothing Anodyne, an identical Charm to Hasten the Night's End in Scroll of Errata, page 156.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:26:28-08:00","id":70345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70326#post70326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overal though, what I hope happens is that medicine becomes less boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, what gives solar medicine its boring feel is that it's not about becoming an awesome doctor; it's about treating all the negative effects in the game system. Its focus isn't thematic, but mechanical.<br /> <br /> You need a charm for every negative effects (poison, disease, crippling, shaping, etc) which leaves less room for charms like Salty Dog Method or Husband Seducing Demon Dance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-12-2014, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:31:07-08:00","id":70346,"title":"","content":"More ideas!<br /> <br /> A charm that provides temporary skill/attribute/health buffs in the guise of herbal supplements! Or longer lasting buffs as long as the user adheres to a specific dietary and exercise regime. If you have to fight all day, or can't find that specific fruit to maintain your Glorious Adonis Physique, then all your power goes away! *edit* Siderealed! dammit!<br /> <br /> Or a charm that debuffs foes if you know what they had to eat! Like some kind of internal alchemy thing. You use a substance that on its own isn't poison but reacts that way with your foes breakfast! Could work as a gas or weapon coating or other kind of poison.<br /> &quot;Tsk tsk, Sesus Lina. You shouldn't have had that chocolate bar for lunch. Especially... WHEN IT REACTS BADLY WITH THE OIL OF THE DUK-TREE SEED! ENJOY YOUR INTESTINAL CRAMPS! AHAHAHAHAHAAA!&quot;<br /> <br /> Okay that last one is probably too specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2258-mrstabs","user":"MrStabs","date":". 02-12-2014, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2258-mrstabs","name":"MrStabs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:39:14-08:00","id":70347,"title":"","content":"Respiration charms for coma-like state. Doubles as a prison Maybe also labour charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","user":"light-hero","date":". 02-12-2014, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:48:04-08:00","id":70351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70341#post70341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind-Soothing Anodyne, an identical Charm to Hasten the Night's End in Scroll of Errata, page 156.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean more like dispelling UMI/NMI, Purity of Mind Method from DB's Medicine can already do this and the charm's fluff look vanilla enough to be a Solar charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:59:55-08:00","id":70356,"title":"","content":"I seem to have rather unpopular views on medicine. :P I kinda like the impressive, lay on hands cure everything no matter what you could do if you stacked the medicine tree in ex 2nd ed. :P<br /> I'm actually torn on using medicine charms for causing harm. While it makes logical sense to me, it also feels a little weird at the same time. I don't actually like the idea of solar versions of it, myself.<br /> I'm also not entirely fond of moving the actual making of medicines and poisons into medicine. Usually, you'd have both, yes, but there are plenty of fantastic doctors who have no idea how there medicines are actually made. (Then again, that might be a modern vs midieval thing. The less advanced, the more sense to connect them, I guess.) Nonetheless, brewing potions feels less charm-y to me.<br /> <br /> That said, I kinda want to second the votes for a fertility type charm, and the immunity bolstering type charms, as well as the charms targeting individuals vs groups. Weaker group heals seems like a cool thing to have, and certainly could make an impression. IMO, Solars have always been very go big or go home, so being able to do more mass heals seems like it should totally be a thing.<br /> <br /> Sorry for not having anything original to add, but I did want to add my two cents, since I do have a character that has the entire medicine tree, heh.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2259-auroradragonkaya","name":"auroradragonkaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2259_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T23:03:47-08:00","id":70359,"title":"","content":"So, Solars are generally where the Christian Religious Miracle stuff goes, if it's applicable. As such, I want to discuss Lazarus.<br /> <br /> Now, first, I get the whole &quot;No Resurrection&quot; and &quot;No Take-backs&quot; thing. I'm good with that. I don't really want to see Solars getting Rez as an essence 4 charm, diamond dust or not.<br /> <br /> And, between the Abyssals, Ghosts, and Liminals, you've got most of the classic &quot;come back to life/visit the underworld and try to bring someone back&quot; themes covered. I get this.<br /> <br /> However, I still want to discuss Lazarus.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not a biblical scholar, but, my understanding of the story is that, while Jesus was out healing the sick and bringing hope to everyone, one of his relatives became ill. Now, had Jesus been there, he could have cured it trivially, but it took too long for the messenger to find him and for them to get back, so Lazarus was dead when they arrived. Then, Jesus tells him to get up and, after some prodding, Lazarus does. This is, iirc, the only recorded instance of anyone coming back to life in the Bible, other than Jesus.<br /> <br /> Now, looking at that, I'm... not entirely sure anything can be done with it, without functionally making death as cheap as it is in D&amp;D. Yet ...I dunno. Once in an entire game feels like it could work. On the other hand, mugging a guy for xp for a one use charm, even one like this, seems crass.<br /> <br /> I dunno. I mean, I'm sure the situation is going to happen in games where Medicine is important. The Solar Healer fails to get there in time to save someone and it's depressing. Is there a way that a Solar can say &quot;...No. NO! I am GOING to SAVE this Person and I don't CARE if it's IMPOSSIBLE!&quot; and have it actually work, without it being either a Liminal's backstory or breaking the setting in half?<br /> <br /> Even if you can't do it as a Medicine charm, I'm curious if the Sorcerous Workings System could be used for this sort of &quot;Once per Game&quot; type effects that have huge emotional and narrative impact, but only if ever done once.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I just wanted to raise the issue, to make sure it was considered, because I'm curious if there might be something useful there, even if it seems like a mire of potential problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T23:11:18-08:00","id":70364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70345#post70345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, what gives solar medicine its boring feel is that it's not about becoming an awesome doctor; it's about treating all the negative effects in the game system. Its focus isn't thematic, but mechanical.<br /> <br /> You need a charm for every negative effects (poison, disease, crippling, shaping, etc) which leaves less room for charms like Salty Dog Method or Husband Seducing Demon Dance.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's the pinnacle of &quot;I can't feel like a great artist if I have Painting Mona Lisa Prana.&quot;, yeah, I can see that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T23:12:23-08:00","id":70365,"title":"","content":"I'd like some passive benefits for just knowing the Charms, perhaps. Such as being able to feel the 'sickness' in a building or forest, the sickness being a magical curse or some such...perhaps the prolonged taint of a demon or abyssal.<br /> <br /> I also think it would be cool to violently rip the infection or disease out of someone, and fashion a temporary weapon out of it. Ripping out a magical disease gives artifact stats. :.D Though, this may be more in line with Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Abyssals, though I know its probably too early to talk about them, but It'd be cool to see a Charm for them that allows them to heal everyone of a single disease (or many, depending on power), but sacrificing someone else. One person becomes a beacon, and draws the disease out of everyone else into himself, killing him instantly, but technically curing the others.<br /> <br /> I've given no large amount of thought to the aforementioned ideas. Hope they lead somewhere good, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T23:30:55-08:00","id":70369,"title":"","content":"Medicine is one of the few places where I'd like to see a definite break from the &quot;Bronze/Iron Age&quot; setting. While certainly beyond the capability of most mortal doctors, I do want things like organ transplants to exist in setting, just being something that only Exalted doctors can successfully perform with any real frequency. Someone has cancer? They don't get chemotherapy, but they do go to their doctor for acupuncture along certain chakra nodes every week. Generally speaking, if it's a medical technique that we can perform in our modern world, I want to see some sort of equivalent in the Exalted setting.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* To note, a lot of these techniques would require Exalted to perform and be will out of reach of the &quot;common man.&quot; Still, if a Dragon Blooded or wealthy merchant prince had cancer, or needed a transplant or a skin graft or whatever, he could find treatment. For most people though, your average &quot;doctor&quot; wouldn't be able to do much more than set bones, perform some basic acupuncture or advise people on a diet to try and balance their chakras.*EDIT*<br /> <br /> So, that said. The number one thing I want to see revolving around Medicine charms. I want the game to make a decision - should there be &quot;instant&quot; healing, or should healing take awhile? And then I want it to stick with that decision. In 1st and 2nd edition, healing was intended to take time; there wasn't supposed to be a Lay on Hands or Cure Wounds spell. But, after the core book, other splats got Lay on Hands charms and eventually so did Solars quickly ruining the &quot;No Instant Healing&quot; rule that was supposed to be a central statement the game made. So if you guys go with a similar statement, make sure not to break it.<br /> <br /> Now for specific charms,.<br /> <br /> As for charms themselves I definitely want a &quot;Surgeon Needs No Tools&quot; type ability - manga like Blackjack or Franken Fran are often my go-to inspirations for Solar medicine capabilities and in many situations they quickly perform amazing medical surgeries with extremely limited tools.<br /> <br /> The idea of a &quot;vaccination&quot; effect that can be used to provide a person with bonuses vs disease or poison is pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Certainly the idea of &quot;offensive&quot; Medicine charms is cool. We've seen a few before such as in the Abyssal book or the Dragon Blooded book.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I'll think of some more ideas, but these are some of the bigger ones I had off hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-12-2014, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T23:38:11-08:00","id":70373,"title":"","content":"Just tossing ideas out there at this point, but &quot;Essence Meridians&quot; might be a cool concept to work with, going along with the Chinese medicine idea where medicine can work its way in to all facets of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T23:38:53-08:00","id":70374,"title":"","content":"Count me in on the &quot;Lay on Hands is actually kind of cool&quot; side. Although, more exotic treatment methods wouldn't go amiss.<br /> <br /> Other than that, though?<br /> <br /> There's really only two things I really <i>want</i> out of Solar Medicine with all else being extra goodies.<br /> <br /> I want the ability to treat a large number of people without eating up my entire mote pool. After a big battle, a Solar Doctor strides through the battlefield and the field hospitals going from one patient to the next and treats them all with supernatural skill, or a wandering Twilight comes upon a village beset by plague and treats every last villager from the seniors down the to children and does so in a single night.<br /> <br /> My other, and personally more major, desire is also simple. What I want is that the only concern of a Solar Doctor is &quot;Is my patient alive?&quot; That's the only thing they need out of them. For them to be alive. Other that? They can be burned, they can be crippled, they can be poisoned, they can be sick, they can be insane, they can be twisted and corrupted by the Wyld or by foreign magicks, or any other form of aliment imaginable or all at once. But so long as they're alive, a Solar can heal them and make them as healthy as they've ever been, if not more so.<br /> <br /> As long as there's life, there's hope. And hope is all a Solar needs to heal someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T23:45:06-08:00","id":70377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70369#post70369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medicine is one of the few places where I'd like to see a definite break from the &quot;Bronze/Iron Age&quot; setting. While certainly beyond the capability of most mortal doctors, I do want things like organ transplants to exist in setting, just being something that only Exalted doctors can successfully perform with any real frequency. Someone has cancer? They don't get chemotherapy, but they do go to their doctor for acupuncture along certain chakra nodes every week. Generally speaking, if it's a medical technique that we can perform in our modern world, I want to see some sort of equivalent in the Exalted setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe available for Merchant Princes, Dynasts and Patricians, or via the rare Solar miracle-healer - but in general, the very ancient world feel of a populace at the mercy of the elements (not just the literal five Elements) is a pretty central part of the setting.<br /> <br /> I'm cool with Terrestrial Medicine Charms allowing for something ala chemo-therapy. Someone having to go through the effects of being poisoned in order to recover another ailment is fitting for a Wood Charm. It should perhaps risk killing mortals in its own right though, as a logical restriction that would explain Wood Immaculates not successfully ending disease in important satraps. Solar Medicine Charms can more reasonably just &quot;lay on hands, you are cured&quot; - but Solars' own numbers check the ability of that to quickly change the entire world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T23:55:15-08:00","id":70379,"title":"","content":"On the Lazarus front: a Charm that allows the Solar to begin using it _before they arrive_. It doesn't help if there isn't someone specifically looking for you to cure the disease, but if they are, the patient will only fall into a deathlike coma which keeps them alive _enough_ (assuming you agree to commit the motes when the person starts looking - which you have to do with limited information) that they can still be saved if you get there in time (probably a scaling amount).<br /> <br /> Not resurrection! Just preemptive Medicine! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd also like some &quot;I AM A SURGEON&quot; in there... it shouldn't substitute for actual Social Charms, but some incidental minor perks would be nice. Like Sail, Medicine is one of those fringe skills... and its hard to actively use.<br /> <br /> Hrm... yeah, increasing the overall health of a community seems important as an option.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll second the idea that for incurable diseases, even the Solar healer should get &quot;this is how to keep him alive&quot; and &quot;this is what the cure will need&quot;. It's just more interesting... curing normal ailments is fine, but curing ANYTHING takes away story options.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, yeah... the current tree should be *condensed* if anything... having a specific Charm for every keyword just makes it feel like an XP tax. Better to have a broad base Charm and follow-on Charms that expand applicability - a starting Solar Doctor cures a patient, an experienced one cures the entire plague. Or they do it faster, or with less ingredients, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T00:17:07-08:00","id":70386,"title":"","content":"I'd like a charm where a Lunar can reach into someone and yank out diseases, cancers, parasites, and 'evil spirits.' This should cause lethal damage though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70379#post70379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Lazarus front: a Charm that allows the Solar to begin using it _before they arrive_.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a Sidereal charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-12-2014, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T00:17:58-08:00","id":70388,"title":"","content":"A Charm which invokes/emulates Agrippa's fight against the plague, promotes general hygiene, and earns the respect of the sick,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/936-erichzahn","name":"ErichZahn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T00:35:57-08:00","id":70396,"title":"","content":"I'd like to be able to take people who have been mutated and cure them, via appropriately esoteric methods (clearing their chakras, realigning their chi, giving them daily regimens to follow, etc). The fact that the only way to do this in 2E was, as near as I can tell, literally punching it off of them (in another tree entirely), was rather displeasing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T00:55:24-08:00","id":70403,"title":"","content":"Maybe a Charm that can complement Tiger Warrior and other minion training techniques to up attributes or related stats perhaps? Utilizing inner Essence and what not.... maybe even a high level Charm to awaken Essence in mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T01:30:23-08:00","id":70422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70359#post70359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I'm not a biblical scholar, but, my understanding of the story is that, while Jesus was out healing the sick and bringing hope to everyone, one of his relatives became ill. Now, had Jesus been there, he could have cured it trivially, but it took too long for the messenger to find him and for them to get back, so Lazarus was dead when they arrived. Then, Jesus tells him to get up and, after some prodding, Lazarus does. This is, iirc, the only recorded instance of anyone coming back to life in the Bible, other than Jesus.<br /> <br /> Now, looking at that, I'm... not entirely sure anything can be done with it, without functionally making death as cheap as it is in D&amp;D. Yet ...I dunno. Once in an entire game feels like it could work. On the other hand, mugging a guy for xp for a one use charm, even one like this, seems crass.<br /> <br /> I dunno. I mean, I'm sure the situation is going to happen in games where Medicine is important. The Solar Healer fails to get there in time to save someone and it's depressing. Is there a way that a Solar can say &quot;...No. NO! I am GOING to SAVE this Person and I don't CARE if it's IMPOSSIBLE!&quot; and have it actually work, without it being either a Liminal's backstory or breaking the setting in half?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Solar physician bring someone back from the dead? Nope. Dead is dead.<br /> <br /> Can you replay the story of Lazarus? Sure, more or less! The poor man isn't <i>actually</i> dead; he's simply so close to death that none of his fellows can perceive his weak and fading vital signs. But the Solar physician can, and her transcendent skill can save his life!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T01:31:13-08:00","id":70423,"title":"","content":"First, let me present my bias regarding the field of medicine. I don't like modern medicine and its primarily because of my experience with surgery(or lack thereof as the case may be). Doctors have told me several times that I need to remove vestigial organs because I don't need them and they are making me ill. I always rejected this approach because I had Chinese practitioners in my family (guess that reveals my origins a bit) that would cure me through some other method, whether that be holistic concoctions or acupressure (a slightly less acute method than acupuncture). My problem is that all my experiences with modern medicine have failed me (unless they resorted to &quot;just cut it off or out&quot;), whereas the other approaches I mentioned earlier seemed to work just fine.<br /> <br /> When I heard about the rejection of common applications of science to explain the setting and the reduction of artifice and other scientific based wonders, I made the assumption that medicine would also be mythic (for lack of a better term). To me, medicine is just a term used to describe that which transforms health. For example, breathing in certain ways is a &quot;medicine&quot; to improving overall vigor in the body. With that in mind, here is what I would like to see and not see.<br /> <br /> I don't want to see a scientific or advanced approach to medicine because I feel that would conflict with other elements of the game that you have already described.<br /> I don't want medicine to be restricted to the specific area of just removing afflictions, diseases, and other debilitating effects.<br /> I do like some of the ideas already presented regarding concoctions and the creation of external medicines, hence I also think medicine charms should cover internal ways of improving health.<br /> In keeping with medicine as being a tool, it can be used for good or ill. It might also be nice if it could scale to the point where a solar could unleash a plague or create a space in which illness and the like can never exist. <br /> <br /> I look forward to how you will shape the philosophy of medicine for mortals, exalted, spirits, demons, and stranger things still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T01:48:06-08:00","id":70433,"title":"","content":"When I payed my Dawn caste doctor, one thing I wanted was an ability to work triage on a battlefield.<br /> <br /> Either a way for the Solar herself to treat a large number of patients or a way to give some of her power to her assistants who can then disperse and heal multiple patients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T01:53:29-08:00","id":70434,"title":"","content":"I like the ideas about making medicines and potions proposed in this thread, but I feel like it should be something mortals can do as well. It makes sense; medicine men and wise witches should be possible without Exaltation, I feel, as every village will be interested in having someone of that skill set. Of course, a mortal may create something that might just help normal recovery rolls while a Solar would make penicillin, but they should have the option, I feel.<br /> <br /> I'm also very interested in the suggestion that have been made about knowledge-related Charms. Knowing the human body (which can help in both aiding and harming it), and knowing healing plants and similar sound like very good ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T02:19:24-08:00","id":70443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70374#post70374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want the ability to treat a large number of people without eating up my entire mote pool. After a big battle, a Solar Doctor strides through the battlefield and the field hospitals going from one patient to the next and treats them all with supernatural skill, or a wandering Twilight comes upon a village beset by plague and treats every last villager from the seniors down the to children and does so in a single night.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can kinda do this with Solar Medicine in Ex2, if you have Miracle Worker's Redemption then everytime you restore someone HL you regain 2 motes, the only problem is that the charm sit smugly at Essence 5 though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like to be able to take people who have been mutated and cure them, via appropriately esoteric methods (clearing their chakras, realigning their chi, giving them daily regimens to follow, etc). The fact that the only way to do this in 2E was, as near as I can tell, literally punching it off of them (in another tree entirely), was rather displeasing. </div> </div> </div>If you don't mind fanwork then Revlid errata Science of Mutation into a Permanent charm that allow you to treat mutation as Crippling effect that can be cure by Wholeness-Restoring Meditation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T03:04:35-08:00","id":70454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70422#post70422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Solar physician bring someone back from the dead? Nope. Dead is dead.<br /> <br /> Can you replay the story of Lazarus? Sure, more or less! The poor man isn't <i>actually</i> dead; he's simply so close to death that none of his fellows can perceive his weak and fading vital signs. But the Solar physician can, and her transcendent skill can save his life!</div> </div> </div> </div>What about some effect whereby the Solar hero can commit motes to stop a patient from dying until the Solar can get to them and try to heal them, potentially with an upgrade charm that lets you activate this as soon as you hear they're ill no matter how far away they are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2260-wurzel","name":"Wurzel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T03:13:49-08:00","id":70459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70386#post70386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a Sidereal charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Sidereal Medicine is nothing like that.<br /> <br /> Even more irritatingly, well...<br /> <br /> Prayers are a real thing in the setting. If Solar-Jesus is being prayed to to help, there is actually already-in-the-setting way for the message to reach them. Actually...<br /> <br /> <br /> Sleep of the Deathless <br /> (costs and stuff)<br /> Even when the Solar cannot provide a cure immediately, they can buy time to seek a solution. This Charm can only be used on a willing or unconscious target, and immediately puts the recipient into a deathlike coma state as long as the motes remain committed. While comatose, the subject can be mistaken for a corpse, but a flicker of life still clings to them. Whatever affliction or injury is killing them is put into abeyance, increasing the length of time between checks to see if the subject dies by a factor of ten times the Solar's Essence. <br /> <br /> Whispers of the Dying<br /> (costs and stuff)<br /> Prereq: Flawless Diagnosis Technique<br /> The Solar's awareness of sickness, disease and injury is transcendent, able to sense subtle changes in the life of people at vast ranges. The range of Flawless Diagnosis Technique increased by a factor of the Solar's Essence, or becomes infinite if the afflicted individual or someone is physical contact with them is praying to the Solar (specifically) to come and cure them. If the Solar knows Sleep of the Deathless, it's range is also increased.<br /> <br /> <br /> There we go. I want THOSE two Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T03:44:20-08:00","id":70461,"title":"","content":"I'm on the fence about this.<br /> <br /> I think Exalted really has to decide whether it wants to play the mythic part straight, or whether it wants to subvert it. Because the same thing happaned back in Performance thread and it's still unresolved. It seems everybody has different ideas on what should be mythological and make sense in a parable sort of way and what parts of mythic narrative should be subverted.<br /> <br /> It seems that the best way would be to subvert those parts of mythology that try to exploit atrocities and play straight the parts that just try to explain the World with a clever narrative that lacks a lot of depth, but is very entertaining. But mythology being so murky and not having a clear divide between the two parts, is really hard to work with!<br /> <br /> It seems that people will trip over this forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T03:45:55-08:00","id":70463,"title":"","content":"What limited knowledge we have of Getimians was something about internal alchemy and internalised looms of fate?<br /> <br /> My knowledge of Chinese medical theory is based solely on Wikipedia but if the info on Getimians is correct then Neidan and Waidan (internal and external alchemy) may fall under their thematics?<br /> <br /> Don't know if that would stop Solars utilising similar ideas though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T04:31:41-08:00","id":70481,"title":"","content":"I see people asking for a &quot;Doctor Needs No Tools&quot; Charm and, well, 2e already has one. Contagion Curing Touch (and Instant Treatment Methodology if you want the extremely-quick part of it). Actually, here's a quick reference to what 2e already has:<br /> <br /> -Negate penalties from Sickness/Poison/Crippling/wound.<br /> -Treat in unfavorable conditions, without medicines/penalties/stunt (aka equipment).<br /> -Heal damage straight-up.<br /> -Grant bonus health levels.<br /> -Convert agg to lethal.<br /> -Diagnose perfectly.<br /> -Treat derangements.<br /> -Cure any Sickness.<br /> -Cure any Poison.<br /> -Cure any Crippling.<br /> -Cure a specific disease within miles, make it into a plague god.<br /> -Add/remove mutations.<br /> -Gain motes/reduce Limit from doing medicine.<br /> -Preserve youth.<br /> -Do an hour of medicine in seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T04:36:54-08:00","id":70486,"title":"","content":"I felt that the 2e set was overly mechanistic, but I will say that I liked its focus on the act of being a supercharged mundane healer, as opposed to 1e's tree which kind of obscured that element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T04:57:07-08:00","id":70496,"title":"","content":"In Pre-Modern days, one of the worst things a person could go through was amputation, but any kind of surgery was hellish because anesthetic did not exist at the time.<br /> <br /> Thus, a charm in which you can poke a person and prevent them from feeling pain during the surgery would be a boon for a field medic. It could also have combat uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T05:00:37-08:00","id":70497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70422#post70422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Solar physician bring someone back from the dead? Nope. Dead is dead.<br /> <br /> Can you replay the story of Lazarus? Sure, more or less! The poor man isn't <i>actually</i> dead; he's simply so close to death that none of his fellows can perceive his weak and fading vital signs. But the Solar physician can, and her transcendent skill can save his life!</div> </div> </div> </div>As always, the Princess Bride proves to be an excellent source.<br /> &quot;He's dead. He can't talk.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot; Whoo-hoo-hoo, look who knows so much. It just so happens that your friend here is only MOSTLY dead. There's a big difference between mostly dead and all dead. Mostly dead is slightly alive. With all dead, well, with all dead there's usually only one thing you can do.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What's that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Go through his clothes and look for loose change.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1397-parallel","name":"Parallel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T05:11:08-08:00","id":70504,"title":"","content":"I want to write this down before I forget it, so I'm posting it before I check and see if someone has beaten me to it: do we have Charms to promote mental health in other beings? Psychology Charms to remove derangements or mental influence, or Charms that affect a being's spiritual health, which I guess you'd represent by maybe boosting Essence regeneration outside of combat timing or something?<br /> <br /> Now to go through three more pages and see if I need to delete this post.<br /> <br /> EDIT: God damn it. Both my ideas, right there at the top of the third page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 02-12-2014, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T05:31:53-08:00","id":70511,"title":"","content":"This has probably been covered, but maybe the line of charms subverting a disease? Curing a disease and using it to spread the cure through transmission? Or giving a temporary buff to whoever had been afflicted with the disease? It calls to mind the idea of a corrupt, diseased wracked town suddenly becoming strong and healthy and throwing off the bonds of their oppressors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2258-mrstabs","name":"MrStabs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T05:35:33-08:00","id":70515,"title":"","content":"Reverse the effects of ageing, Artifact organ translplants, healing a community or a congenital defect in a family, passing gently into lethe, triggering terrestrial exaltation, finding the medicinal properties in non established medical plants, mineral reagents, contolling dieases spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T06:07:52-08:00","id":70525,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say without knowing what the rules for poison, disease, maiming, etc. are like.<br /> <br /> How about basic sanitation effects? Stuff like cleansing infected water or rotten meat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T06:25:34-08:00","id":70533,"title":"","content":"I wonder where young-restoring and immortality effects will sit on the Essence scale, since those effect was regarded by the book as being very rare and powerful, Solar need Essence 7 for the young-restoring effect while Immortality require a 5-level Manse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-12-2014, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T06:28:04-08:00","id":70536,"title":"","content":"Something written somewhere that will actually help you fix/ help with a wide scale epidemic.<br /> <br /> Felt kinda powerless when i can only heal like 5 people a day in a city of thousands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2129-steel_in_sea","name":"Steel_in_sea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T06:40:01-08:00","id":70541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70496#post70496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Pre-Modern days, one of the worst things a person could go through was amputation, but any kind of surgery was hellish because anesthetic did not exist at the time. Thus, a charm in which you can poke a person and prevent them from feeling pain during the surgery would be a boon for a field medic. It could also have combat uses.</div> </div> </div> </div> We already have exactly that: Touch of Blissful Release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T06:49:58-08:00","id":70542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steel_in_sea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70536#post70536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something written somewhere that will actually help you fix/ help with a wide scale epidemic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some kind of reverse epidemic, a harmless disease that fights off the current plague?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T06:53:30-08:00","id":70544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steel_in_sea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70536#post70536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something written somewhere that will actually help you fix/ help with a wide scale epidemic.<br /> <br /> Felt kinda powerless when i can only heal like 5 people a day in a city of thousands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finding &amp; fixing the source of a disease/poison and being able to spread a cure the same way an epidemic spreads would both go a long way toward allowing for stories of Solars riding into town to heal a dying populace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:04:38-08:00","id":70561,"title":"","content":"Probably been mentioned before, but I'd love to play a Solar doctor who can supplement his fighting style with weaponized acupuncture and such. Abyssals shouldn't have all that fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:26:42-08:00","id":70578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine#post70267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any requests?<br /> <br /> Please try not to ask for things that are already in the 2e set.</div> </div> </div> </div>John,<br /> <br /> One of the major issues I had with 2e medicine was the distinction between MENTAL and PHYSICAL health.<br /> <br /> Exalted needs to kinda take a stance on an issue we haven't figured out entirely in the modern day, which is to say... how much does biology play into things like madness?<br /> <br /> Can you cure a derangement with medicine?<br /> <br /> If not, how do you cure a derangement? Via presence and Freudian analysis?<br /> <br /> Both methods make powerful arguments about the way Exalted treats neurosis and, well, people in general.<br /> <br /> In 1e (and 2e) the only real methods of interacting with mental issues that I recall are in the Dragonblooded charmset, which always struck me as very weird.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice to have some sort of system for quantifying mental strain / madness and methods of interacting with that mechanic that were more defined and direct.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:26:50-08:00","id":70579,"title":"","content":"I think a Medicine-based Martial Art Style would be balls.<br /> <br /> (&quot;Balls&quot; is good, right? I'm not hip with the lingo.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:35:21-08:00","id":70585,"title":"","content":"Since we're bronze/iron aging here, how about something that fits the thematic of a medicine man? Being able to cure not only the physical and mental ailments of a person but their spiritual ailments as well? Also, as a way to make drugs without having to take craft: the xp sink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/731-lurker","name":"Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar731_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:37:50-08:00","id":70586,"title":"","content":"Maybe something that lets a solar bless a building and infuse it with power in order to mark it as a place of healing. Inside it people heal faster, recover from disease quicker and because it is marked as a place of peace maybe no hostilities can be started inside so long as the mark remains or one medicine man remains to defend it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/777-bronze-tiger","name":"Bronze Tiger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:43:39-08:00","id":70593,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that 'medical treatment' already included making medicine for others, though it didn't provide for gathering any necessary ingredients.<br /> <br /> 'I brew him a healing remedy from the roots of the acafernus plant, sweeten it with honey, and tell him to drink' shouldn't require a craft roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:43:41-08:00","id":70594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lurker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70585#post70585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're bronze/iron aging here, how about something that fits the thematic of a medicine man? Being able to cure not only the physical and mental ailments of a person but their spiritual ailments as well? Also, as a way to make drugs without having to take craft: the xp sink.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another option, certainly.<br /> <br /> My point is that Exalted has to decide if madness...<br /> <br /> A) ... is a biological issue caused by improper physical condition. This is actually how modern science more-or-less understand these things.<br /> B) ... is an emotional condition that cannot be treated physically, only through contemplative growth, healing and self-exploration... (the 'therapist' approach)...<br /> C) ... the consequence of evil spirits invading the body that must be removed (probably the most authentic).<br /> <br /> I don't really have a severe preference here just, we need to get off the fence about it, because mental illness DOES happen in games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:50:17-08:00","id":70600,"title":"","content":"Given the Sail charm preview, I would assume that Medicine can cure mental illness regardles of how it happens, simply because curing illness in general is part of the Medicine archetype.<br /> <br /> Potions, I'm not too sure about. It depends on whether you want folk remedies, which should be under Medicine, unnatural alchemical formluas, which would probably fall under sorcery rather than Craft, or both. I'd personally try to make room for both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:59:30-08:00","id":70607,"title":"","content":"If Solar Medicine Charms are supposed to be &quot;mortal Medicine, but better!&quot; instead of DnD cleric spells, then Touch of Blissful Release and Anointment of Miraculous Health stand out as the two Charms that didn't supplement or replace any mortal Medicine action. Maybe at least place those after the Diagnosis Charm, and possibly Contagion Curing Touch (ie: Doctor Needs No Tools/Medicine).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T08:03:49-08:00","id":70610,"title":"","content":"Both of those would be accupressure.<br /> <br /> Mortal medicine != modern, Western notions of medicine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T08:06:24-08:00","id":70611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70504#post70504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charms that affect a being's spiritual health, which I guess you'd represent by maybe boosting Essence regeneration outside of combat timing or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or curing things that damage or attack the soul, like the ravaging of the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> I'm sometimes torn on that subject, between how I like the idea inherent to Charms to cure poison or crippling effects that are so comprehensive that they can affect purely magical forms of damage as an expression of Solar might, while thinking the alternative would lead to excessively specialized Charms, and wanting to give them more room to veer around in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T08:10:27-08:00","id":70612,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer if the charms did have some basis in the fictional 'reality' of the game. I don't have anything against free-form powers, mind, but just letting a Solar decide that feeding purple gumdrops to a patient is 'in paradigm' and heal them thusly feels to me... I dunno, somehow a cop out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T08:12:54-08:00","id":70613,"title":"","content":"I think there could be Solar Charms to cripple some of a person's senses or bodily functions, like breathing or being able to digest food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T08:21:44-08:00","id":70616,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a medicine charm or two that benefits from friendship ( can't remember if intimacies are still a thing or not). Like being able to treat a circlemate while in combat, because you two have worked together so much, you have an instinct for where to be to not get in the way. Removing wound penalties or committing x motes/willpower to the injured person,not assigning temporary health levels like in 2nd edition, but actually sliding the damage back.<br /> (piss poor example but it's the best way I can try to explain.)<br /> <br /> Battle Hardened Patient Bond<br /> cost: 2m/5m <br /> duration: one scene<br /> The alliances and friendships forged upon the field of battle overcome the strongest foes and bolster through the most grievous wounds. A Solar may activate this charm and direct the effects at an ally whom she has an intimacy towards. for 2 motes she can give up to her Intimacy+Essence in temporary basing health levels. These levels only hold damage that has already occurred, thereby clearing the target's normal health track. Any health levels over the damage taken are converted to bonus dice to the target's next roll to stop bleeding, maintain consciousness, resist poison. For 5 motes per dot, the Exalt can give lethal health levels. The motes spent on this charm are committed until the scene ends, at which point the motes and the damage returns to the normal health track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/841-okamigrif","name":"Okamigrif","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T08:54:26-08:00","id":70631,"title":"","content":"One thing that I would like is for Medicine Charms to matter to the Exalted. Exalts being resistant to disease is great, but if they are straight up immune to most disease then my disease-curing Charms aren't normally of much use to the other players at the table. If a plague-filled city could threaten their lives, then my ability to fix it fast becomes something they value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T09:25:22-08:00","id":70645,"title":"","content":"Well, to get the 2e-ism out of the way first, it's not a medicine charm but rather a part of medicine. I liked and would like to see again is the ability for the player to define how they do medicine. acupuncture, herbalism, using leeches for everything... anything was fair game. I liked that. It allowed you to do everything from the Solar British Sergeant-Major style that shouts at his men until they get better, to the classics like acupuncture all the way to doing drum circles to align spiritual energies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That out of the way, a Solar medical master should have a robust understanding of how people work, be it mentally, physical, emotionally. Indeed, this should spill over to animals, spirits and anything else. They should have an understanding of how organic group systems work, leading them to an understanding of the spread of diseases of the mind body and soul, the natural spread of life in general, be it modeling the growth of a village for the next few decades or the growth of moss on a tree.<br /> <br /> From these concepts, we get into effects. A Solar should be able to restore ability to an old crippled limb, but by the same token they should know exactly where to strike in combat to disable a limb or function. Improve health and condition, the classic healing and medical treatment.<br /> <br /> They should be able to talk with a man or a spirit and in time dig out the causes anger or fears and work with them to sooth them. By the reverse token they should be able to study people and gain insight into their mental and emotional triggers.... such as a gang member's blind hatred of the gang leader and the deep seated desire of the former for the latter's position. Thus giving you the insight that if you take out the leader this other one will step up and his hate will likely keep him from doing what the previous leader thought was a good idea*.<br /> <br /> They should be able to guide the growth of individuals and groups. The whole raise 30 generations of selectively bred plants/animals in an instant kind of thing where you bring forth specific desired traits. There should be the ability to encourage or prevent disease in an area or in a population. To analyse needs and requirements for a desired effect now and in the future... For example, knowing that the animals are doing poorly due to a lack of a particular substance or mineral, and have an idea how it could be addressed. Or what diet to feed them to make the goats far more productive of milk.<br /> <br /> And just as Solars are leaders of men, so too should their medical skills in some case be able to treat collective groups. Curing an individual of a plague is something a skilled mortal can do. Curing a city of the plague is something a Solar should do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Going up against a Solar with a medical focus in a physical conflict should have people quaking in fear. Not because they hit hard, not because they'll convince you to stop with clever words, but because when they do hit you, they know exactly where to hit and in what order to do everything from disable your leg or liver, all the way up to stopping your heart.<br /> <br /> Going up against a Solar with a medical focus in a social conflict should have people quaking in fear. Not because their words are honey'd traps, not because they'll convince you to sell your own grandmother, but because they know every injury done to you by yourself, others or just time. Mental, physical or emotional they can offer you a cure for any or all of it... for a price. Worse it can go in the other direction. Your enemies can be made to suffer plagues, gain addictions to substances you alone control... or worse.<br /> <br /> Going up against a Solar with a medical focus in a kingdom vs kingdom conflict should have people quaking in fear. His people are always at the peak of physical fitness. They have no untreated vices or additions to exploit. They eat better and live without the periodic rampages of terrible disease that cripple other armies. His people are content, have a fantastic quality of life... and are willing to fight anyone that tries to take that from them and their families.<br /> <br /> <br /> *-yes I'm aware this is edging into socialize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T09:35:19-08:00","id":70650,"title":"","content":"I can mostly just second what Odd_Canuck said. This is what I mostly want from medicine, as well. Especially the first two parts about having control on how your mastery of medicine manifests is important to me.<br /> <br /> And I had even written custom charms along of what Canuck wrote about combat applications of medicine, a couple years back.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not a hundred percent sure if this fits Exalted, but I have always missed a plain healing charm, where you spend Essence, and restore someone's health levels in combat time. This is less important to me, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T09:36:33-08:00","id":70651,"title":"","content":"More Medicine Charm Ideas<br /> <br /> * The Solar become extremely adept at handling poisons and diseases you have treated before. Any mundane disease or poison you have successfully treated may be banished from the target with but a touch and a few motes.<br /> <br /> * Guided by her will and intuition, the Solar uses local resources to create a powerful medicine that can be applied to food, drink, crops and so on. Roll Intelligence + Medicine and re-roll X until there are no more X dice. If the roll meets or exceeds the highest (Virulence/Poison) difficulty, all hazardous effects are removed. This is a single application good enough for one person. This Charm can also created enough medicine to effect a large population by adding +Y motes and 1 Willpower. When using the Charm in this fashion, it creates enough medicine to effect up to (meaningful number) people/miles/places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/132-crescens","name":"Crescens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T09:51:32-08:00","id":70661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70578#post70578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cure a derangement with medicine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Misho Thrice-Blessed says it's all just Medicine. Anyone who says otherwise is calling Misho a liar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T09:55:43-08:00","id":70664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70661#post70661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Misho Thrice-Blessed says it's all just Medicine. Anyone who says otherwise is calling Misho a liar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so, but when I call Misho Thrice-Radiant a liar, I at least recall his name (and, of course, why he was named so).<br /> <br /> Facetiousness aside, I can get behind curing Derangements with Medicine, since the other likely candidate for it (social skills) have plenty of cool design space, while Medicine tends to be more limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:06:34-08:00","id":70668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70422#post70422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Solar physician bring someone back from the dead? Nope. Dead is dead.<br /> <br /> Can you replay the story of Lazarus? Sure, more or less! The poor man isn't <i>actually</i> dead; he's simply so close to death that none of his fellows can perceive his weak and fading vital signs. But the Solar physician can, and her transcendent skill can save his life!</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:16:16-08:00","id":70670,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who feel that you shouldn't need Occult, Craft(Water) and the art of Alchemy to create medicine pill or brewing herbal decoction ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:45:11-08:00","id":70695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70670#post70670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who feel that you shouldn't need Occult, Craft(Water) and the art of Alchemy to create medicine pill or brewing herbal decoction ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Medicine-related rituals used Medicine in place of Craft (Water) but required Lore. But no, no you aren't alone in wanting to have the steep number of Abilities required pared down to the logical single example of Medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:45:29-08:00","id":70696,"title":"","content":"Hey I was thinking about this and I just remembered: CHOPPER from one piece. Aside from his diagnostic ability he powers himself via special drugs that interact with his specific physiology. So, maybe the ideas for new cool medicine charms depend on a new element introduced in the setting which medicine charms can interact with. Something like &quot;medical artifacts&quot; or just a good system for potions (not just poisons and toxins). If there's something like an aspirin in creation, a solar can produce a super-aspirin that even grants the user a small version of Ox-Body for a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:46:53-08:00","id":70699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70369#post70369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medicine is one of the few places where I'd like to see a definite break from the &quot;Bronze/Iron Age&quot; setting. While certainly beyond the capability of most mortal doctors, I do want things like organ transplants to exist in setting, just being something that only Exalted doctors can successfully perform with any real frequency. Someone has cancer? They don't get chemotherapy, but they do go to their doctor for acupuncture along certain chakra nodes every week. Generally speaking, if it's a medical technique that we can perform in our modern world, I want to see some sort of equivalent in the Exalted setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70377#post70377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe available for Merchant Princes, Dynasts and Patricians, or via the rare Solar miracle-healer - but in general, the very ancient world feel of a populace at the mercy of the elements (not just the literal five Elements) is a pretty central part of the setting.<br /> <br /> I'm cool with Terrestrial Medicine Charms allowing for something ala chemo-therapy. Someone having to go through the effects of being poisoned in order to recover another ailment is fitting for a Wood Charm. It should perhaps risk killing mortals in its own right though, as a logical restriction that would explain Wood Immaculates not successfully ending disease in important satraps. Solar Medicine Charms can more reasonably just &quot;lay on hands, you are cured&quot; - but Solars' own numbers check the ability of that to quickly change the entire world.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0337.html\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Normal doctors can't cure cancer willy-nilly, Misho.&quot;</a><br /> <br /> &quot;But it's so easy when you know how to do it!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:50:58-08:00","id":70707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70270#post70270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually putting &quot;create new lifeforms&quot; here rather than a separate pseudo-science crafting system could be rather cool, and perhaps less genre breaking than the alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won\u2019t let Medicine handle this alone, but you have given me something to consider, re: created life forms, funerist techniques, etc. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70270#post70270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Fertility Charms might be rather in theme for Solars, given the roles of &quot;Solar Heroes&quot; in myth and ancient religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be awesome or disturbing (or both) depending on how I carry it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70275#post70275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Some sort of vaccination/preemptive antidote effect to bolster others' immunity to getting sick or poisoned would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regular medical treatments can do things like this\u2014Solar Medicine can enhance the accuracy of such treatments. It\u2019s plausible that a Solar could use her Essence to confer greater resistance, enhancing such a treatment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70278#post70278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is using Medicine as a weapon thematically reserved to Abyssal and Sidereal Charms (the latter assuming they're still in Saturn's purview)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I vary on this. If Medicine is comprehensive in its expression of medical disciplines, battle tactics feel like a bit of a stretch. But I want to encourage creative combinations of Abilities (ex: Martial Arts + Medicine).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70281#post70281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've considered wanting a Solar Medicine Charm that inflicts a healing soporific (branching off of Touch of Blissful Release) which not only makes targets tired, but increases their healing rate / makes other Medicine Charms cheaper while they sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of a CB:T Charm. I\u2019ll look into it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70281#post70281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charms for leading a team of medics would be great too.</div> </div> </div> </div>*taps chin* You don\u2019t see this situation commonly in Creation. A Solar putting together a tent city to treat a plague would be a fairly monumental thing. Such a Charm would need to be a very close-proximity one, Solar-to-target enhancement, rather than an improvement of a large group. Such an event needs to retain the challenge in order to maintain drama, and the monumental feeling of what is happening. A Solar creates a bulwark of tents to stop Final Contagion. The withering darkness and the falling death are stayed at its border. Dare the Wyld Hunt burn these tents? Can the Solar possibly save everyone? Can her assistants possibly keep up with the tasks she has given them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70281#post70281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might overlap with Survival (which I'm fine with honestly) but Charms that identify the healing capabilities of natural products would be awesome. I always like Charms that incorporate the environment of a scene like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make a player use Medicine + Lore or Medicine + Survival for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70281#post70281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that reminds me. 2e had these Charms for healing poison/crippling/sickness, and could do it even if there was no cure. While cool, I found them sorta boring in-game. Just boom, done. It might be cooler if there were Charms that many not perfectly cure a patient instantly and right then, but always told you a way how: a special plant, a secret technique, whatever -- something out there, if put into the supernal hands of a Solar medic, would have the capability to cure what would otherwise be incurable. Better adventure fodder that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have given me a lot to think about. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mobius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70284#post70284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see more Medicine charms that enhance their beneficiaries. Rather than merely curing their ails, cure the ails they never knew they had. Fortify their strength with a mixture that seems dubious to those less learned than you. Readjust their chi flow with acupuncture, fortifying their stamina for a time. That sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70289#post70289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a Solar charm that allows you to completely wreck a person, and then make them even stronger than before. There's quite a few Wuxia films where the hero gets stronger because they visited a doctor and acupuncture made them better, or they took some crazy herbal pill and survived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actively modifying another character is a little more complex than what Medicine does on its own and really oughtn\u2019t be handled by a Charm, as it can be the plot of several interesting Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70285#post70285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure 2e doesn't have any &quot;create a medical formula&quot; charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I avoid Charms that neatly resolve epic conflicts or dramatic narratives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70291#post70291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More Charms to cover the healing of psychological damage and/or disorders might be appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll have to think about this one. Creation sees many of these maladies as being spiritual in nature\u2014different spirits affecting the patient\u2019s mind or mood\u2014and that ambiguity is important. That said, we do have derangements in this edition, although they have less modern names. Solars should be able to interact with such things. I\u2019ll think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70318#post70318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see a charm that allows you to commit motes and give someone bonus dice to prevent their disease--or appropriate condition--from getting worse, allowing the patient to survive just a little while longer:<br /> <br /> Hold on! The doctor is on his way!</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70323#post70323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, something not in 2e core.<br /> <br /> I'd like it if the charms worked on both individuals and small groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70323#post70323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, something not in 2e core.<br /> I'd also like a charm that lets me treat the causes of a disease or poison. If the village well has been supernaturally befouled, I'd like a charm that lets me cleanse it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like an interesting story cut short by a Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrStabs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70338#post70338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe something generally health related? Like a supertonic that provides a list of small effects to the user? I remember all these magical fixes and devices sold on the internet and infomercials, so something like a miraculous supertonic seems right up a Solar's ally.<br /> <br /> It could maybe do stuff like:<br /> <br /> -Remove aging penalties to attributes (grandpa goes from boney weak geezer to ULTRABUFF OLD MAN)<br /> -Remove penalties from sleep deprivation/exhaustion<br /> -Removes pain-based penalties from inherited diseases or old injuries<br /> -Increase stamina for long forced marches<br /> -Provide general resistance to non-life threatening disease like colds or flus<br /> -Allow the digestion of foods normally difficult for human digestion (Plant matter, cheap meats, foods that you are alergic to)<br /> -Provide a natural bloom of health to boost appearance-based rolls by a little<br /> -Lets mortals resist infection and staunch bleeding easier.<br /> -Increases fertility and removes possiblity of inherited diseases/conditions passing onto children.<br /> <br /> It'd be a very mortal-centric charm and need balancing to keep from stepping on other charms/splats toes, but a Miraclous Solar Supertonic isn't too different from tiger warrior training in that regard.<br /> <br /> Maybe each supertonic is unique, like picking from a list of effects when it's brewed? Or purchased as a charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some very creative ideas here. I wouldn't have Solars making magic tonics, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70345#post70345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, what gives solar medicine its boring feel is that it's not about becoming an awesome doctor; it's about treating all the negative effects in the game system. Its focus isn't thematic, but mechanical.<br /> <br /> You need a charm for every negative effects (poison, disease, crippling, shaping, etc) which leaves less room for charms like Salty Dog Method or Husband Seducing Demon Dance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70396#post70396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to be able to take people who have been mutated and cure them, via appropriately esoteric methods (clearing their chakras, realigning their chi, giving them daily regimens to follow, etc). The fact that the only way to do this in 2E was, as near as I can tell, literally punching it off of them (in another tree entirely), was rather displeasing.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNoted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70403#post70403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">maybe even a high level Charm to awaken Essence in mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGranting Exaltation is a bit beyond the scope of Medicine. EX3 doesn't have &quot;awakened&quot; mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70403#post70403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a Charm that can complement Tiger Warrior and other minion training techniques to up attributes or related stats perhaps? Utilizing inner Essence and what not.... maybe even a high level Charm to awaken Essence in mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems many people want to be able to treat larger groups. Just remember that execution will be limited to how it pushes realism in Creation. There won't be a Charm to make your nurses just as effective as you, or a Charm to wander across a battlefield Essence-zapping people back to life. Solar Charms thrive on a logos of action and dramatic effect. This is what allows them to be so powerful. Taking away the need for logos does make them more powerful, but it also makes them into miscellaneous wish-powers, which by turns makes them uninteresting, boring, and disappointing. So my challenge here will be to make it so that you can luxuriate in the extremely difficult challenge of triage, rather than just hope your Athletics and Awareness Charms can get you where you need to go fast enough and your Medicine Excellency will help you when you get there. A large part of this is going to be on you, and the Storyteller. Making things interesting requires a little elbow grease and creative use of the system and Abilities at large. No Charm, no matter how well written, will ever suffice.<br /> <br /> \u200b <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wurzel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70454#post70454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about some effect whereby the Solar hero can commit motes to stop a patient from dying until the Solar can get to them and try to heal them, potentially with an upgrade charm that lets you activate this as soon as you hear they're ill no matter how far away they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars can\u2019t bring characters back from narrative death, but they can bring them back from mechanical death. Look forward to seeing suspended death / induced coma and \u201cshe is not dead\u201d as a mechanical \u201cthing\u201d Solars can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wurzel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70454#post70454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about some effect whereby the Solar hero can commit motes to stop a patient from dying until the Solar can get to them and try to heal them, potentially with an upgrade charm that lets you activate this as soon as you hear they're ill no matter how far away they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLong ago, I once wrote a Charm called A Hood on Death. It was very boring. Charms shouldn\u2019t replace certain stories. \u201cThe search for a cure\u201d is one of those stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70578#post70578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> John,<br /> <br /> One of the major issues I had with 2e medicine was the distinction between MENTAL and PHYSICAL health.<br /> <br /> Exalted needs to kinda take a stance on an issue we haven't figured out entirely in the modern day, which is to say... how much does biology play into things like madness?<br /> <br /> Can you cure a derangement with medicine?<br /> <br /> If not, how do you cure a derangement? Via presence and Freudian analysis?<br /> <br /> Both methods make powerful arguments about the way Exalted treats neurosis and, well, people in general.<br /> <br /> In 1e (and 2e) the only real methods of interacting with mental issues that I recall are in the Dragonblooded charmset, which always struck me as very weird.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice to have some sort of system for quantifying mental strain / madness and methods of interacting with that mechanic that were more defined and direct.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I recently decided to add derangements to the system. But when I encountered them, I came up against the issue of &quot;What people think they are&quot; vs. &quot;What they really are.&quot; Many believe that such malaise is caused by an evil spirit nesting in the mind and leaving some of its tainted Essence there. It is highly likely that 99.9% of causes are biological, but in a world like Creation, there can always be a spiritual or esoteric cause. Just note that changing a person\u2019s biology is not a common or easy effect, nor should it be. Thanks for helping me organize that thought.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bronze Tiger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70586#post70586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe something that lets a solar bless a building and infuse it with power in order to mark it as a place of healing. Inside it people heal faster, recover from disease quicker and because it is marked as a place of peace maybe no hostilities can be started inside so long as the mark remains or one medicine man remains to defend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool idea, but it strikes me as a spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70612#post70612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer if the charms did have some basis in the fictional 'reality' of the game. I don't have anything against free-form powers, mind, but just letting a Solar decide that feeding purple gumdrops to a patient is 'in paradigm' and heal them thusly feels to me... I dunno, somehow a cop out.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agree.<br /> <br /> Okay, thanks for your feedback everyone. You have given me a lot to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:54:01-08:00","id":70710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70544#post70544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finding &amp; fixing the source of a disease/poison and being able to spread a cure the same way an epidemic spreads would both go a long way toward allowing for stories of Solars riding into town to heal a dying populace.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much what I want btw. 2nd ed had solar's who could defeat armies by themselves, or convert entire towns to a cause, but medicine never really had the equivalent. Sure, they could cure something incurable, but they couldn't do anything on any sort of mass scale, while other solars could. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2259-auroradragonkaya","name":"auroradragonkaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2259_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:55:29-08:00","id":70711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70422#post70422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Solar physician bring someone back from the dead? Nope. Dead is dead.<br /> <br /> Can you replay the story of Lazarus? Sure, more or less! The poor man isn't <i>actually</i> dead; he's simply so close to death that none of his fellows can perceive his weak and fading vital signs. But the Solar physician can, and her transcendent skill can save his life!</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e, at least, a Labyrinth Necromancer can bring someone back for a few moments...and an Abyssal Necromancer could bring them back for a few minutes. It would be an interesting interplay to see a Solar use some potent Charm to strengthen the black ties that are holding a person's soul together, and allow them to live longer. Of course, it would probably wreak havoc on that persons mental well-being... ...but if you REALLY don't want someone to die, within those precious few minutes that they've been dead, well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:59:45-08:00","id":70716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>auroradragonkaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70710#post70710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty much what I want btw. 2nd ed had solar's who could defeat armies by themselves, or convert entire towns to a cause, but medicine never really had the equivalent. Sure, they could cure something incurable, but they couldn't do anything on any sort of mass scale, while other solars could. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars built the Realm Defense Grid which cured the Great Contagion across Creation. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:02:59-08:00","id":70717,"title":"","content":"I think that before medicine charms can be created, it would be good to consider where the cut-off point is for mortal medicine, especially with thaumaturgical support. Are potions and realigning essence flows more effective in a mortal's hands than surgery? Can they be made to be more effective if you know the secrets of Alchemy?<br /> <br /> Then supercharge that. Like, allow a Solar doctor the ability to create uber potions out of the usual materials and so on.<br /> <br /> IIrc, in previous editions, medical technology was such that getting surgery was mostly just a complicated form of murder unless you had an Exalt working on you. But poisons and diseases could potentially be partially to completely cured, depending on how good at herb lore (or Alchemy) the local healer was. I'm curious if this will remain the same in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:07:19-08:00","id":70719,"title":"","content":"One effect I'd like to see would be a &quot;tracking patient zero&quot; kind of thing. Once you diagnose the problem with a person, you could identify the <i>cause</i> of that problem - the particular poison thorn that stabbed them, the individual rock that broke their ankle, the specific other person who infected them with the disease. That would let you trace infections back to their sources, figure out who stabbed your patient, and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:08:54-08:00","id":70720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70717#post70717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIrc, in previous editions, medical technology was such that getting surgery was mostly just a complicated form of murder unless you had an Exalt working on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is fairly historically accurate... its also quite funny for some reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:10:10-08:00","id":70723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70707#post70707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars can\u2019t bring characters back from narrative death, but they can bring them back from mechanical death. Look forward to seeing suspended death / induced coma and \u201cshe is not dead\u201d as a mechanical \u201cthing\u201d Solars can do.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X90qKQAMh8A\" target=\"_blank\">It just so happens that your friend here is only <i>mostly</i> dead.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:19:06-08:00","id":70727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70716#post70716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars built the Realm Defense Grid which cured the Great Contagion across Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>But was that something built by solar doctors, or solar sorcerers? If the latter, how does this affect the feel of those dedicated to medicine?<br /> <br /> (That said, making the Realm Defense Grid be less destructive is interesting, if that's where you're going with it!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2259-auroradragonkaya","name":"auroradragonkaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2259_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:19:35-08:00","id":70728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70716#post70716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars built the Realm Defense Grid which cured the Great Contagion across Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>With respect, John, I can see how someone who set out to make the Ultimate Doctor might be annoyed to learn that the Ultimate Feat Of Doctordom is best accomplished noth through Medicine, but through Craft - especially given how many other things Craft is the best tool for.<br /> <br /> Granted, the Realm Defense Grid also drove off a Creation-wide invasion, allowed for the greatest consolidation of power in Creation's history \u200band contained the borders of the Wyld, and I don't expect to see anyone complaining that this means Craft trumps Melee, Socialize, or Sorcery. Clearly, the Grid goes beyond what even a Solar do unaided, and that's cool. But just as a lone Solar can (with difficulty and often at personal cost) head off an army or sway the hearts of a nation, I would like for a Solar doctor to have ways to fight off a city-wide pestilence, even if it still needs time or benefits strongly from mortal helpers.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of making medicines or cleansing areas for this - the first gives you a solution, but you need to distribute it (which could run into interference from gangs or local customs, involving allies and other PCs), while the second requires you to do some legwork to find out where the disease is more prevalent and you'll probably need to hit multiple &quot;sources of corruption&quot; with a deadline, lest the ones you've already cleansed develop a new population of disease spirits or what have you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:47:27-08:00","id":70745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70664#post70664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe so, but when I call Misho Thrice-Radiant a liar, I at least recall his name (and, of course, why he was named so).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very rude of you to ruin my jokes by pointing out that I already ruined the joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:48:32-08:00","id":70746,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to add that, while no one wants a magic plot saving cure all, not being able to do enough can have the same effect. Not being able to deal with minor, mundane afflictions without burning your motes and having a highly compassionate character (Whether one uses the virtue system or not) can be crippling. Sorry, I'm twiddling my thumbs now because I wasted 3 will and 30 motes to heal 3 random mooks in terrible condition during an earthquake isn't very satisfying, but equivalents have happened in games I've been in.<br /> Meanwhile, the social solar can talk down 3 random mooks without batting an eye, same for the combat monkey. That's kinda one of the problems with medicine, I think. It's hard to do scaling with it, and differentiate major storyline from not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2259-auroradragonkaya","name":"auroradragonkaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2259_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:56:54-08:00","id":70749,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain I'm going to get it anyway, but far and away the biggest thing I want out of medicine in 3e compared to 2e is that we don't have an artifact that replicates 80% of the functions of the core solar medicine tree. That was something that always rather annoyed me. I could spend 100+ XP to be the greatest solar healer... or I could spend 12 XP for an artifact that covers 80% of the same effects if a bit slower.<br /> <br /> Sorry to bring it up, and like it's already unlikely to be an issue but every time I think of medicine in 2e.... Arrrragh. And it is one of my favorite abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:09:05-08:00","id":70763,"title":"","content":"I think that the more robust and elegantly-designed the system for disease and injuries is (or how robust and elegantly-designed the basic task resolution mechanics are) will have a big effect on how fun Medicine Charms are to use. &lt;/statement of the obvious&gt;<br /> <br /> Looking at the 2E corebook Medicine tree, it seems basically adequate. I think that Contagion-Curing Touch was probably not the best way to model &quot;Solars can do their work even in difficult situations&quot; - there's definitely room for that sort of effect, but &quot;you can do even more stuff with a stunt&quot; might have been better than &quot;you don't need to stunt anymore.&quot; IDK.<br /> <br /> So, I guess, some things it might be cool to see from 3E (a lot of these are probably not universal enough to warrant a slot in the Corebook, admittedly ^^<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><ul><li>Charm to aid in my diagnoses (or at least to prevent misdiagnoses).</li> <li>Charm building off of it that makes serious health problems stand out to my Solar like they're lit up with neon: they'd be like a cancer-sniffing dog, or able to tell that someone was healing from a stab wound just based on their body language, or able to detect the signs of a &quot;social disease&quot; as soon as the next morning. Assessment of peoples' health would become almost automatic and reflexive, so perceptive would be the Solar doctor.</li> <li>I'll also second Chejop Kejak's request for more general information-gathering Medicine Charms that let my Solar tell things like what position an athlete plays based on which of his muscles are the most developed, or someone's entire medical history based on the taste of their sweat or the smell of their breath, or similarly wild stuff.</li> <li>Charm to increase the effectiveness with which the Solar can formulate their own medicines - maybe that's more appropriate in Craft, IDK, or could be cross-prereq'd or something, but &quot;Hermit Joe's Miracle Swamp Weed Tea&quot; should totally be a thing my Twilight can formulate.</li> <li>Maybe not some sort of effect that just straight-up cures diseases or removes poison, at least not early on in a tree, but something that buffs up a Solar doctor's ability to fortify their patient's own strength for the purposes of rolls to fight off infection/poison/the influence of malevolent spirits/etc. or battle their way back from the brink of death.</li> <li>Some sort of &quot;in the zone&quot; Charm that allows a Solar to push through hunger, fatigue, pain, their own illness, distractions, and so on as long as they're devoting their full attention to caring for those who need their medical help. &quot;The only time the legendary dragon-chaser Huo Sixth-Beard could resist the call of the opium pipe was when some poor soul was bleeding on his operating table...&quot; - y'know?</li> <li>Acupressure!! Obviously actually messing with other characters' Essence respiration is probably detrimental to fun, so this would require some careful design, but Solar Medicine should totally let you suss out the Essence flows along the meridians of living creatures - even spirits. Might aid in the diagnosis of any detrimental supernatural effects that are afflicting a character? Possibly build into some sort of &quot;sense the Essence of living creatures as glowy silhouettes on your HUD&quot; effect, if that's appropriate?</li> <li>I think it was in Fringe that I saw this - at one point a shapeshifting character had to break the bones of their face so they could reknit it into a new appearance. There was also a wuxia film (I think it was &quot;Judge Dee and the Phantom Flame&quot;?) where a few of the characters did similar face-changing shenanigans with acupuncture. I don't know if that would be a Charm on its own, but it'd be cool for Solars to be able to do something like that, if only as part of a broader cosmetic-surgery Charm. Gotta disguise Jim Kirk as a Romulan!</li> <li>Maybe some sort of &quot;independent automatic treatment&quot; effect - like, you give someone a prescription or a diet/exercise regimen and if they follow it, it's like they have you assisting their treatment rolls for whatever malady afflicts them except you don't actually have to do anything. This could obviously upgrade into Medicine-based Training effects based on healthy living and internal alchemy.</li> <li>Someone suggested a &quot;Don't worry, I'm a doctor!&quot; effect that allowed a Solar to confidently seize command of a medical emergency, and I think that's really cool. It could also build into an effect that allows a Solar doctor to dispel a patient's fear and panic with their masterful bedside manner.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:30:20-08:00","id":70779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70594#post70594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's another option, certainly.<br /> <br /> My point is that Exalted has to decide if madness...<br /> <br /> A) ... is a biological issue caused by improper physical condition. This is actually how modern science more-or-less understand these things..</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr. My understanding is that modern science (in as far as there is a consensus on these things) holds that it's a lot more complicated than a simple biological cause in quite a few situations. There are cases where there is something biologically wrong and that's mostly it, but there are also cases where it's a complex interaction of biology, personal history and social surroundings (this isn't an argument in favour of psychoanalytic approaches, mind, as they tend not to work) -- this is why you can sometimes control an illness with drugs combined with an approach like cognitive behavioural therapy, or (in mild cases, speaking from personal experience) with CBT-type approaches alone.<br /> <br /> Some statistics via a psychology grad student friend of mine regarding schizophrenia, which is one of the illnesses most generally held to be strongly biological:<br /> <br /> 1) Identical twins have only a 50% chance of developing schizophrenia if one of them does. They share the same biology, so environment and social factors are just as important as biology.<br /> <br /> 2) In treating schizophrenia, drugs and other purely biological approaches are actually some of the least efficient if used alone. Family therapy, where the family of the patient undergo therapy together with the patient, reduces the relapse rate from 75% (if using drugs alone) to 50%, and CBT even more so.<br /> <br /> Modern science does not understand mental illness as having purely biological roots. (I can get citations if you want.)<br /> <br /> Basically, Solar medicine should cover therapy as well -- it shouldn't be conflated with psychoanalysis; it isn't a scam. It's one part of the full suite of approaches to tackling a very difficult problem even in cases when its grounded in biology, and an approach to mental illness that ignores it in favour of a purely mechanistic 'brain fix' also isn't playing up to the notion of a Solar healer as a <i>healer</i>, rather than a neurosurgical technician or exorcist. (And it also fails to do justice to the experiences of mentally ill people.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: There are also issues arising in cross-cultural psychiatry regarding this kind of thing, but this post is complicated enough. There's an interesting and tragic case study of this sort of issue in Anne Fadiman's <i>The Spirit Catches You and You Fall Down</i>, about the interaction of an epileptic child of Hmong refugees with the US medical system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":978,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","user":"Iozz-Sothoth","date":". 02-12-2014, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:30:43-08:00","id":70780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70717#post70717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that before medicine charms can be created, it would be good to consider where the cut-off point is for mortal medicine, especially with thaumaturgical support. Are potions and realigning essence flows more effective in a mortal's hands than surgery? Can they be made to be more effective if you know the secrets of Alchemy?<br /> <br /> Then supercharge that. Like, allow a Solar doctor the ability to create uber potions out of the usual materials and so on.<br /> <br /> IIrc, in previous editions, medical technology was such that getting surgery was mostly just a complicated form of murder unless you had an Exalt working on you. But poisons and diseases could potentially be partially to completely cured, depending on how good at herb lore (or Alchemy) the local healer was. I'm curious if this will remain the same in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>BR really has a good point here that I don't want to get lost in the shuffle - previously, Occult suffers from a lot of this, as well. Whatever the medicine system is, I sincerely hope it's not an isolated system from mortal medicine, but rather an extension of it... just something Solars do amazingly well, rather than another miracle entirely that a mortal doctor wouldn't understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:33:11-08:00","id":70782,"title":"","content":"I should add that my thinking about how medicine should work in games has been strongly influenced by <i>Legends of the Wulin. </i>In that system, recovering from injuries (or any number of other conditions) is actually a series of die rolls. Anyone trained in Medicine can give you an assistance bonus to your rolls to recover from injury, and someone actually trained in the Secret Art of Medicine (i.e. wielding Charms) gives you the assistance bonus <i>and</i> allows you to use the better result of your roll to heal and their roll to treat your injuries on recovery checks.<br /> <br /> I think it would be cool if Exalted represented that sort of cooperative effort between doctor and patient a little. Adds drama, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:41:04-08:00","id":70787,"title":"","content":"Nothing to add, just kind of shocked that this question is just now being asked. With the continued push back of the game, I would have thought this would have been covered a while ago. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:52:32-08:00","id":70791,"title":"","content":"For someone reason some sort of &quot;pressure point&quot; stuff would be neat. Not sure it would be Medicine and not say Martial Arts, but being the doctor who freezes people up or Vulcan Grips people to calm them down always seemed appropriate to me. About all I can think of off the bat.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:53:21-08:00","id":70792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70610#post70610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of those would be accupressure.<br /> <br /> Mortal medicine != modern, Western notions of medicine.</div> </div> </div> </div>But neither of them are mortal actions within the system.<br /> <br /> Not unless the merely mortal version of Touch of Celestial Bliss is giving someone a massage... or handjob.<br /> <br /> But that still leaves Anointment of Miraculous Health. What kind of mortal action is THAT based on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:54:11-08:00","id":70795,"title":"","content":"To answer the question, again I tend to think in abstracts. I want Solar medicine to be awe-inspiring. The charms in 2nd Ed aren't great because being nested in the core book. They give the impression that these are the norm or the standard. We don't get a great look at regular medicine so Solar medicine seems to be all that matters. I am not a fan of that. <br /> <br /> Something can only be amazing in the context of the mundane. Give me more on how the human world functions. Why are Solars so impressive? Can this feel be expressed beyond &quot;kewl&quot; powers? <br /> <br /> I recently fell in love with Solars again. I want their abilities to be amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:56:13-08:00","id":70798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HokyoRoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70787#post70787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing to add, just kind of shocked that this question is just now being asked. With the continued push back of the game, I would have thought this would have been covered a while ago. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>It has. Now a developer is asking fan base opinions to see if their view and ideas cover what other people think are core elements of the ability or not. Helps tighten up the quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T13:03:35-08:00","id":70802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70798#post70798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has. Now a developer is asking fan base opinions to see if their view and ideas cover what other people think are core elements of the ability or not. Helps tighten up the quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess. A year and some months after announcement and several push backs already. That seems off to me. I also notice that as time goes on, I find my excitement for 3rd ed waning. What was a strong desire to play is now a mild interest because far too much time has passed. I had originally planned to run my Solar game I am running into third but it has taken so long, that we did something else.<br /> <br /> Again, don't mind me. Just pointing out something that seems bothersome. If I am the only one. I am fine with that. It just makes me sad because as a contributor to the Kickstarter. I expected more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T13:04:30-08:00","id":70803,"title":"","content":"I think one of the big things the system needs to decide is, &quot;How bad, to a Solar doctor, is a plague?&quot; In 2e, a cholera epidemic was basically unmanageable by a Solar physician - or, more to the point, his Solar Medicine didn't allow him to do anything to manage it that a mortal couldn't already. Sure, you could cure a dozen people a day with confidence, but if the plague is sweeping across a decent-sized nation... well, it's not going to make much difference, is it? A Solar dropped into the middle of Black Death-ridden Europe is not, <i>medically</i>, going to be much help, at least pre-A Hood on Death.<br /> <br /> (The Solar may rally the people, institute new sanitation standards, etc., but that's a function of rather different Charm trees, one imagines.)<br /> <br /> The question, for me, is: to what extent is that the intent? Should I be able to protect my people from plague? It feels like the answer to this should be <i>yes</i> - so, all right, how? What does large-scale Solar medicine look like?<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> Practically, if you're playing a Solar doctor, you have pretty decent odds of starting with the declaration, &quot;I want to be House&quot; - or insert characters from ER, etc. And House is interesting because he <i>struggles</i> with disease - because there's work involved in figuring out what's wrong and setting it to rights. Solar Medicine should definitely make that struggle easier, or make possible things that weren't previously... but in 2e, there's an awful lot of &quot;and the problem is solved!&quot;-type effects that don't really contribute to feeling like you worked for your victory.<br /> <br /> There's definitely a place for that - splinting a broken leg should be pretty trivial. But there needs to be some more meaningful system of struggling with disease - perhaps, as previously suggested, something that requires you to hunt down the cure, or a Medicine Charm that tells you, &quot;The city is befouled by bad air, because it's stuck in a valley; to alleviate this, let the wind blow through it once again.&quot; People viewing it from the outside should feel like you did something impossible with ease; actually <i>doing</i> it should still feel like you're working.<br /> <br /> That's not really anything concrete, I guess, but it's where my mind goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T13:29:34-08:00","id":70817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, that reminds me. 2e had these Charms for healing poison/crippling/sickness, and could do it even if there was no cure. While cool, I found them sorta boring in-game. Just boom, done. It might be cooler if there were Charms that many not perfectly cure a patient instantly and right then, but always told you a way how: a special plant, a secret technique, whatever -- something out there, if put into the supernal hands of a Solar medic, would have the capability to cure what would otherwise be incurable. Better adventure fodder that way. </div> </div> </div> To add to this, if you ever read Monster Hunter International series, the Orcs each get one gift they are great/phenominal. Gretchen has the ability to heal but each poltice is unique to the individual and and wound. Thus not only would the above charm be better adventure fodder, but once used on the Super Great Contagion, you do not have a cure-all for everyone who catches it but only a cure to that specific individual and to cure another individual of the Super Great Contagion you would need different ingredients/rituals/stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>while (horse.state == dead)<br /> {<br /> beat();<br /> }","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/830-amdramnar","name":"Amdramnar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T14:15:28-08:00","id":70833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HokyoRoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70787#post70787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing to add, just kind of shocked that this question is just now being asked. With the continued push back of the game, I would have thought this would have been covered a while ago. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>The Medicine tree was done-ish some time ago (enough that they could have released it along with everything else if Rich had denied them the opportunity to give the Charms another pass), but Hatewheel has been revising all the charm trees and adding stuff. You can chart the progress of the trees he's revising on the Monday Morning Meetings.<br /> <br /> Remember that the charm trees are traditionally one of the very last things done, and that (with the possible exception of Craft) the revisions have largely been done in order of how much playtesting they're likely to need, so that the ones that need the most have the most test cycles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T14:50:11-08:00","id":70864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe so, but when I call Misho Thrice-Radiant a liar, I at least recall his name (and, of course, why he was named so).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70745#post70745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is very rude of you to ruin my jokes by pointing out that I already ruined the joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're being nitpicky, I think that <i>strictly</i> speaking, his proper name is Thrice-Radiant Misho, and not the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T14:53:20-08:00","id":70866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70864#post70864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're being nitpicky, I think that <i>strictly</i> speaking, his proper name is Thrice-Radiant Misho, and not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>BAM! I just got out-nitpicked. Well played.<br /> <br /> Serves me right for only referencing <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0335.html\" target=\"_blank\">one comic </a>to check my memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:08:02-08:00","id":70874,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>auroradragonkaya</b> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">This is pretty much what I want btw. 2nd ed had solar's who could defeat armies by themselves, or convert entire towns to a cause, but medicine never really had the equivalent. Sure, they could cure something incurable, but they couldn't do anything on any sort of mass scale, while other solars could. :/</span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <b>Statement:</b> Solars can do X but they can't do Y.<br /> <br /> <i>Originally posted by <b>John M\u00f8rke</b></i><br /> <i>Solars built the Realm Defense Grid which cured the Great Contagion across Creation.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Response:</b> But Solars can do Y. See example Z.<br /> <br /> A less tongue-in-cheek response: Spending 10m, 20m, 30m, to end threat because you bought End Threat Prana is boring. Somewhere along the lines the Solars had to think about building things that could deal with issues on a scale larger than the person to person basis of Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:22:22-08:00","id":70886,"title":"","content":"I think what's somewhat disappointing about Medicine, at least as previously presented, is that it is indeed person-to-person. When you use Craft, it can range from a minor trinket to a Realm Defense Grid. Medicine doesn't seem to scale in any kind of way. It's mostly confined to &quot;healing, but faster or better.&quot; And it only moves in an upward progression rather than outward. Some doctors make house calls, others research permanent cures, and others go to plague-ridden villages to clean them up &amp; heal the populace. While building a machine that can cure an entire area of a contagion is a great story, so is using one's personal medical acumen to achieve the same result. Your argument seems to be, and correct me if I'm wrong, that being able to do the former precludes being able to do the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:32:02-08:00","id":70889,"title":"","content":"That and, as demonstrated, a lot of theoretical Medicine charm concepts are inherently things that close off stories. No need to SEARCH for a cure to someone's disease if you have a CHARM that can cure that disease. Granted, maybe the players aren't INTERESTED in that story because it's a wide tangent from the story they came for, but even so, it makes Medicine a bit landmine-ridden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:35:13-08:00","id":70890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70707#post70707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*taps chin* You don\u2019t see this situation commonly in Creation. A Solar putting together a tent city to treat a plague would be a fairly monumental thing. Such a Charm would need to be a very close-proximity one, Solar-to-target enhancement, rather than an improvement of a large group. Such an event needs to retain the challenge in order to maintain drama, and the monumental feeling of what is happening. A Solar creates a bulwark of tents to stop Final Contagion. The withering darkness and the falling death are stayed at its border. Dare the Wyld Hunt burn these tents? Can the Solar possibly save everyone? Can her assistants possibly keep up with the tasks she has given them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Building a tent city as a bulwark against the Final Contagion should be as dramatic and engaging as raising an army to face off against the Hordes of the Last Ones.<br /> <br /> My thoughts were more along the line of up to a half dozen-or-so assistants, however. Still, you wouldn't want Charms that just go &quot;boom! you're awesome at medicine!&quot; even to a half dozen folk, because that's also boring. I've given it some thought, and there's ways I think you could have interesting, engaging Charms for uplifting medical assistants.<br /> <br /> For example, a Charm that improved assistants that have watched and helped you work, and have an Intimacy toward you (you've worked together for years and know each other's strong and weak points; now as a Solar, that synergy is even greater), and/or an Intimacy toward a specific patient (the patient's mother/son/husband stands by worried as you work; you show them some of your ways, and they take it to heart for the sake of their loved one). The former encourages you to build relationships with your long-term assistants, while the latter lets you leave capable nurses in your wake, making sure your patients survive even after you ride out of town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","user":"Limited Reagent","date":".  sometimes I suck at typing 02-12-2014, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:45:59-08:00","id":70894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70890#post70890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. Building a tent city as a bulwark against the Final Contagion should be as dramatic and engaging as raising an army to face off against the Hordes of the Last Ones.<br /> <br /> My thoughts were more along the line of up to a half dozen-or-so assistants, however. Still, you wouldn't want Charms that just go &quot;boom! you're awesome at medicine!&quot; even to a half dozen folk, because that's also boring. I've given it some thought, and there's ways I think you could have interesting, engaging Charms for uplifting medical assistants.<br /> <br /> For example, a Charm that improved assistants that have watched and helped you work, and have an Intimacy toward you (you've worked together for years and know each other's strong and weak points; now as a Solar, that synergy is even greater), and/or an Intimacy toward a specific patient (the patient's mother/son/husband stands by worried as you work; you show them some of your ways, and they take it to heart for the sake of their loved one). The latter encourages you to build relationships with your long-term assistants, while the other lets you leave capable nurses in your wake, making sure your patients survive even after you ride out of town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good, good. Thanks for your input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:46:53-08:00","id":70895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70886#post70886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what's somewhat disappointing about Medicine, at least as previously presented, is that it is indeed person-to-person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how avoidable that is, though. Medicine is about specific knowledge and techniques to apply that knowledge, which is very personal in scale. Unless you create a Charm to imbue others with some of your skill so they can help out (Glorious Solar Nurse?), applying Medicine on a broad scale strikes me, someone who has no idea what the mechanics currently look like, as something more akin to sorcery than Medicine Charms.<br /> <br /> On topic, though, how <i>about</i> a Charm that lets you empower a helper? Is that too Dragon-Blooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:58:48-08:00","id":70898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70874#post70874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A less tongue-in-cheek response: Spending 10m, 20m, 30m, to end threat because you bought End Threat Prana is boring. Somewhere along the lines the Solars had to think about building things that could deal with issues on a scale larger than the person to person basis of Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hurm, I can see this and agree with it. However you'll have to forgive us as it's all very very new conceptually. The idea of a Solar making something in 2e to see to the health or well being of a large number people isn't something that was address that I can recall in 2e. Well, outside of &quot;really big gun to protect people by shooting&quot;. <br /> <br /> The closest I can think of to an artifact or structure that was to help mortals would be the jade obelisks or the manse power to produce food. Which, while they're great in themselves are not exactly about medicine health or well being beyond &quot;I don't want Creation warped by the wyld&quot;. Oh, and possibly the ward against disease, but they were very narrow in application and required the ability to craft artifacts plus the relevant procedure of Creation.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that we can look forward to artifacts manses or other things that *are* made for preventing disease, healing wounds and so forth on a large scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T16:23:14-08:00","id":70905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70898#post70898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hurm, I can see this and agree with it. However you'll have to forgive us as it's all very very new conceptually. The idea of a Solar making something in 2e to see to the health or well being of a large number people isn't something that was address that I can recall in 2e. Well, outside of &quot;really big gun to protect people by shooting&quot;.<br /> <br /> The closest I can think of to an artifact or structure that was to help mortals would be the jade obelisks or the manse power to produce food. Which, while they're great in themselves are not exactly about medicine health or well being beyond &quot;I don't want Creation warped by the wyld&quot;. Oh, and possibly the ward against disease, but they were very narrow in application and required the ability to craft artifacts plus the relevant procedure of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't know about that. I'm in a high-Essence game defending Gem where the crafters are busily working on civic and defence projects like a Sky Mantis Tower and various mundane contraptions to solve the water problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T16:23:49-08:00","id":70906,"title":"","content":"A lot of people seem to want a Medicine Charm to help home in on vulnerable parts of enemies. I always wanted a Charm to help keep my enemies alive more easily, either by avoiding those lethal spots or focusing on parts that disable rather than kill. If the previewed Salty Dog Method is any indication, maybe a Permanent, early-tier Medicine Charm that gives a number of basic benefits can include that a Solar doctor knows how to inflict nonlethal damage on any strike that isn't, say, made out of sunfire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1135-zan","name":"Zan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T17:21:39-08:00","id":70934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70898#post70898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hurm, I can see this and agree with it. However you'll have to forgive us as it's all very very new conceptually. The idea of a Solar making something in 2e to see to the health or well being of a large number people isn't something that was address that I can recall in 2e. Well, outside of &quot;really big gun to protect people by shooting&quot;.<br /> <br /> The closest I can think of to an artifact or structure that was to help mortals would be the jade obelisks or the manse power to produce food. Which, while they're great in themselves are not exactly about medicine health or well being beyond &quot;I don't want Creation warped by the wyld&quot;. Oh, and possibly the ward against disease, but they were very narrow in application and required the ability to craft artifacts plus the relevant procedure of Creation.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that we can look forward to artifacts manses or other things that *are* made for preventing disease, healing wounds and so forth on a large scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're asking if I'm going to mechanize solutions for massive problems that have haunted Creation since day one... no, not at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T17:26:34-08:00","id":70937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70707#post70707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some very creative ideas here. I wouldn't have Solars making magic tonics, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be a tonic. It could be a treatment or acupuncture session. I kinda latched onto the idea of a snake oil salesman whose snake oil actually does what he says it does. At least I've got an NPC for my next Exalted game!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the response, John. Super pumped for Exalted 3rd!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2258-mrstabs","name":"MrStabs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T18:04:18-08:00","id":70944,"title":"","content":"I assume that if the Realm Defense Grid helped treat the Great Contagion, it was not made by a single Solar with Craft and Occult but no Medicine. It was likely made by a large number of high-level Exalts, some of whom were medical experts.<br /> <br /> I don't think it takes away from Solar doctors any more than eyeglasses take away from real world optometrists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-12-2014, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T18:12:19-08:00","id":70946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70886#post70886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what's somewhat disappointing about Medicine, at least as previously presented, is that it is indeed person-to-person. When you use Craft, it can range from a minor trinket to a Realm Defense Grid. Medicine doesn't seem to scale in any kind of way. It's mostly confined to &quot;healing, but faster or better.&quot; And it only moves in an upward progression rather than outward. Some doctors make house calls, others research permanent cures, and others go to plague-ridden villages to clean them up &amp; heal the populace. While building a machine that can cure an entire area of a contagion is a great story, so is using one's personal medical acumen to achieve the same result. Your argument seems to be, and correct me if I'm wrong, that being able to do the former precludes being able to do the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, other way around: if you can do the latter, doing the former is pointless and stupid.<br /> <br /> If you can just wave your giant golden wang in the air and solve the problem, there's no story, no interaction, no nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, I agree with dev.. Medicine shouldn't scale up past the village-or-so level - past that point, it's not a job for one person, it's a job for a LOT of people. <br /> <br /> Charms should let you do the impossible by doing the difficult, they shouldn't make things effortless unless it's okay to have the effortlessly done things no longer matter to the story.<br /> <br /> I mean, you roll up a Solar Doctor, you want stories about your doctoring. Not just &quot;yep, everyone I met ends up in perfect health, no muss no fuss&quot;. So yeah... focus on curing the incurable in an interesting fashion, in increasing longevity and productivity through superior health... on being the Court Physician, not an entire health industry in the shape of one person. (Maybe sneak a &quot;falling for the nurse&quot; Charm effect in somewhere too...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T18:29:52-08:00","id":70955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70944#post70944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that if the Realm Defense Grid helped treat the Great Contagion, it was not made by a single Solar with Craft and Occult but no Medicine. It was likely made by a large number of high-level Exalts, some of whom were medical experts.<br /> <br /> I don't think it takes away from Solar doctors any more than eyeglasses take away from real world optometrists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly so!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T18:35:14-08:00","id":70956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70433#post70433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I payed my Dawn caste doctor, one thing I wanted was an ability to work triage on a battlefield.<br /> <br /> Either a way for the Solar herself to treat a large number of patients or a way to give some of her power to her assistants who can then disperse and heal multiple patients.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant to quote Kunoichi earlier, in my big post, but the forum software wisely decided I was quoting someone else. Anyway, this was for you, Kunoichi:<br /> <br /> It seems many people want to be able to treat larger groups. Just remember that execution will be limited to how it pushes realism in Creation. There won't be a Charm to make your nurses just as effective as you, or a Charm to wander across a battlefield Essence-zapping people back to life. Solar Charms thrive on a logos of action and dramatic effect. This is what allows them to be so powerful. Taking away the need for logos does make them more powerful, but it also makes them into miscellaneous wish-powers, which by turns makes them uninteresting, boring, and disappointing. So my challenge here will be to make it so that you can luxuriate in the extremely difficult challenge of triage, rather than just hope your Athletics and Awareness Charms can get you where you need to go fast enough and your Medicine Excellency will help you when you get there. A large part of this is going to be on you, and the Storyteller. Making things interesting requires a little elbow grease and creative use of the system and Abilities at large. No Charm, no matter how well written, will ever suffice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T18:43:27-08:00","id":70959,"title":"","content":"A lot of the 2E stuff felt as fire-and-forget and impersonal as a Potion of Cure Moderate Wounds, despite being among the most overtly miraculous parts of the Solar charm set. It sounds like you're already planning on making that more dynamic, but one thing I'd especially like to see 3E Solar Medicine do is leave a <i>lasting social impression</i>.<br /> <br /> Medical Caregivers in real life often inspire <i>awe and devotion</i>, especially if the condition successfully treated was disabling, disfiguring, or chronic. This can be as minor as a plate of brownies dropped by the ER, or as major as a new lifelong friend, but just as often it's not welcomed <i>at all</i> by the caregiver. One of the guys in my cancer support group had a restraining order against him by two surgeons and an <i>anesthesiologist </i>(don't ask, I never opted to explore that rabbit hole). When a Solar uses his &quot;Cleanse Leper&quot; charm, the beneficiary will probably be more inclined to attend one of his Sermons, at the very least. Also any close friends or family of that ex-leper. And a fair number of unrelated bystanders who saw it happen.<br /> <br /> But what if that Solar isn't hosting sermons, he's trying to keep a low profile? That is a dude who does <i>not</i> need a fledgeling Cult singing his praises. Even if he has the right Social Traits and inclination to direct them towards his own purposes, that's the kind of social movement that the serious <i>old school</i> Wyld Hunt rides out for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:21:24-08:00","id":70973,"title":"","content":"One thing I would like to see, if not a Charm that helps you mass-cure, then a Charm that allows a Solar's presence in an area act as a beacon of hope, giving everyone within the city/town/whatever bonuses to resist whatever malady is threatening them. This way a Solar's legend as a healer can help the sick and wounded fight off the worst, but the Solar still has to perform the actual act of healing in order to guarantee everyone else gets better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:23:52-08:00","id":70975,"title":"","content":"While instantly zapping people with golden medical knowledge is pretty boring, i would think that a Tiger Doctor Training charm would be in theme, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/855-magistrate","name":"Magistrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:30:00-08:00","id":70979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magistrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70975#post70975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While instantly zapping people with golden medical knowledge is pretty boring, i would think that a Tiger Doctor Training charm would be in theme, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am hesitant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:33:06-08:00","id":70982,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that be covered by the 3E Harmonious Academic Methodology? Granted, it's not a medicine charm, but it fills more or less the same function of teaching people how to be good healers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:37:00-08:00","id":70983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70982#post70982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that be covered by the 3E Harmonious Academic Methodology? Granted, it's not a medicine charm, but it fills more or less the same function of teaching people how to be good healers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:39:42-08:00","id":70984,"title":"","content":"I would think that actually imparting &amp; training others would be under Harmonious Academic Methodology/Legendary Scholar Curriculum while running a medical facility (or similar) would fall under Bureaucracy, Presence, and Socialize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:05:44-08:00","id":70992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magistrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70975#post70975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While instantly zapping people with golden medical knowledge is pretty boring, I would think that a Tiger Doctor Training Charm would be in theme, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had in mind a more temporary effect, boosting your assistants only for as long as you have motes committed and extending their ability to work and excel under pressure, or to act as your proxies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:22:46-08:00","id":71003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70956#post70956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant to quote Kunoichi earlier, in my big post, but the forum software wisely decided I was quoting someone else. Anyway, this was for you, Kunoichi:</div> </div> </div> </div>Why thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> It seems many people want to be able to treat larger groups. Just remember that execution will be limited to how it pushes realism in Creation. There won't be a Charm to make your nurses just as effective as you, or a Charm to wander across a battlefield Essence-zapping people back to life. Solar Charms thrive on a logos of action and dramatic effect. This is what allows them to be so powerful. Taking away the need for logos does make them more powerful, but it also makes them into miscellaneous wish-powers, which by turns makes them uninteresting, boring, and disappointing. So my challenge here will be to make it so that you can luxuriate in the extremely difficult challenge of triage, rather than just hope your Athletics and Awareness Charms can get you where you need to go fast enough and your Medicine Excellency will help you when you get there. A large part of this is going to be on you, and the Storyteller. Making things interesting requires a little elbow grease and creative use of the system and Abilities at large. No Charm, no matter how well written, will ever suffice. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I totally agree that just using a charm to clap your hands and sunburst-heal a battlefield would be an impressive power, but a kind of dull one. I can think of a couple different ways off of the top of my head (maybe the middle of my head since I've pondered this before).<br /> <br /> 1) The Solar has her patients gathered and continually moves between them, both observing their conditions and intervening medically when necessary. It could be limited to a number of patients or could be limited geographically (as in, anyone within your move distance). Heck, if you did it the second way, then the Solar could keep it up for longer than the typical hour and have new patients brought in once the previous ones are stabilized or cured. Granted, this could leave it open for abuse by untiring Solars becoming a medical factory.<br /> <br /> 2) Second idea, one I actually just thought of would be to have the Solar begin treatment of someone, then they have an assistant take over and the Solar's healing continues (for the hour or whatever) while the Solar can leave and do other things, potentially visiting others and healing them. I imagine it would work via committed motes for the assistant and the Solar could keep visiting new patients and assigning &quot;nurses&quot; to them as long as she wants to keep motes committed (assuming committed motes still exist). I actually like this idea quite a bit as it ensures that the Solar sees each individual patient and it sort of seems like reality with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:23:35-08:00","id":71004,"title":"","content":"I just realized something kind of neat as a way to transfer knwoeldge would be to write prescriptions that work fairly great for a disease, sending it off with someone to implement the stuff needed to treat it. I also think some form of long-distance analysis and diagnoses based on minimal data is pretty genre-appropriate.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:44:34-08:00","id":71017,"title":"","content":"Well, the peek we got at Sail Charms makes it seems like it is potentially okay for an Abilitiy's Charms to slightly infringe on other abilities' territories, as long as it thematically limited by the Ability to which the Charm actually pertains and the sort of legend that Ability is intended to portray.<br /> <br /> Just like being the Legendary Sailor involves more than being awesome at boat-driving, including effects that touch the thematic space of Athletics, Survival and maybe others, being a legendary doctor might include some secondary social or bureaucracy effects that apply to the limited circumstances that reflect the legend of the great healer.<br /> <br /> Though I imagine Sail is a bit unusual in having more of this kind of effect than other abilities, due to the problems it used to face of lack of applicability in many games, leaving Eclipses with a useless Ability (Specially since they also have Ride, which was the one that became useless in many West-based games).<br /> <br /> <br /> As for my own interests in the Medicine Charms, much was already said (and expressed better than I could). Still, I'd like to emphasize my interest in preventive medicine being a thing that Charms could help. This has to do with a tidbit my acupuncture teachers have told me: in ancient times, many acupuncturists who were responsible for a given village's health would get paid (likely periodically) only as long as the people were healthy. If they got sick, the acupuncturist was not paid for that period.<br /> <br /> (many times have I heard &quot;the bad acupuncturist heals the disease. The good acupuncturist doesn't let it happen in the first place&quot; *)<br /> <br /> So, yeah, dietary, hygienic, exercise and other regimens, along with preventive therapy (stimulation of specific chakras, unblocking meridians, massages, counseling and so on) to get people to be resistant to illness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">Which sometimes makes me feel bad, since usually people only come to me after they are already ill. Very, <i>very </i>few people come to me when they feel relatively fine for me to take preventive measures before minor imbalances become major ones, opening the doors to illness</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:55:27-08:00","id":71026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70281#post70281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be cooler if there were Charms that many not perfectly cure a patient instantly and right then, but always told you a way how: a special plant, a secret technique, whatever -- something out there, if put into the supernal hands of a Solar medic, would have the capability to cure what would otherwise be incurable. Better adventure fodder that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a major problem with these kinds of effects.<br /> <br /> Here's the issue: You've basically just described a &quot;find plot&quot; charm. That is to say that the only real effect a charm like this has is to ask the ST to give you the plot.<br /> <br /> In practical terms it does nothing. If nobody in the circle had any medical knowledge, and a vital character was sick, the ST would give us a way to go on a quest to save them regardless -- we wouldn't be using our own personal medical knowledge in any way, but if it were important to the players or the overarching plot, we would be able to go somewhere and find something or someone that would at least give us a <i>chance</i> at success. Don't say that it shouldn't work like that, or that the problem is STs who run things like that; that's how it does work and everyone knows it. Saying &quot;no, what you want is totally impossible&quot; is boring when you can say &quot;here is an epic quest to attempt that!&quot; And because setting you on an epic quest is something that every ST is going to want to do and is going to always be trying to do, you should never charge XP for a charm whose only effect is to provide the initial direction that sets you on a quest.<br /> <br /> If you doubt it, consider this: What would a non-Solar circle do -- a circle of some splat that lacks these sorts of medicine charm -- if they had someone with a horrific disease who needed curing? I can tell you what they would <i>not</i> do: Give up and shrug because you need Medicine to even attempt an epic quest to cure someone. So... what exactly does a Twilight doctor contribute to the situation, then? You might tell the doctor ,in my previous example, &quot;well, you didn't buy the plot-hook finding charm, so Tiny Tim dies&quot;, but you obviously wouldn't say that for a circle that never had the <i>option</i> to buy that charm... and since most players are going to be aware of this, it makes the charm feel like a waste of XP at best.<br /> <br /> In my experience -- I've played games with powers like those before, powers that are basically &quot;summon plot hook.&quot; And every single time, even when I used them, it left me with a very unsatisfied taste in my mouth. Why did I take that charm? Everyone at the table is aware that I just wasted XP and motes (or whatever the resources were in that game) to get what the ST was going to give us for free anyway. Why didn't I spend that on something useful? Leaping over mountains and cutting the tops off mountains are cool because they are tools that I, as a player, can assemble to find my own solution to tasks; they interface with the world in a dynamic fashion, in a way that leapfrogs off my other powers (and the contributions of the rest of the table) to face and overcome challenges.<br /> <br /> &quot;Enable epic quest&quot; charms are worthless. You don't need a charm for that.<br /> <br /> (This doesn't mean that your medicine charms have to be able to cure everything, of course. I'm just saying that &quot;point you in the direction of a plot device&quot; is not, itself, a meaningful power worth spending XP on; it could be a flavorful side-effect to a charm whose practical mechanical applications are elsewhere, maybe when you activate it for something it can't cure. But it shouldn't be considered a meaningful part of a charm's value, because practically speaking most of the time it just reflavors the source of a plot hook you would have encountered anyway.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-12-2014, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:56:03-08:00","id":71028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70934#post70934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're asking if I'm going to mechanize solutions for massive problems that have haunted Creation since day one... no, not at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Give mechanics for no, give some indication in the setting of, yes. It should be treated like any other great wonder of the past. Just having such things exist *for this purpose* is very much a new thing.<br /> <br /> However your statement of &quot;have haunted creation since day one&quot; part makes me wary, as it implies it's always been a problem and even in the first age the Solars were able to do nothing about up-scaling their powers in this field. Which now has me somewhat turned around and confused, since it would be like saying &quot;yes the solars were capable of doing great things and made great wonders to do even greater things on a larger scale, except medicine of course.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:58:56-08:00","id":71031,"title":"","content":"While this might be Lore, I'd like to see more psychotherapy charms. Especially a charm that could let you engage in psychotherapy as social influence and / or in combat.<br /> <br /> As much as I love Hastening the Night's End, it only works on willing volunteers - and if you use Presence charms on a villain they may be willing but did not volunteer, so the charm ends. I need an anti-madness charm that could be used on the unwilling as a form of influence or combat would be great. There are some villains who can only be helped this way (The Joker from DC is a good case in point.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T21:14:30-08:00","id":71032,"title":"","content":"something like the ability of accelerator to deactivate the bomb in the head of last order (toaru majutsu no index) but medicine oriented<br /> <br /> things to discern and treat mental diseases","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T21:26:06-08:00","id":71033,"title":"","content":"Regarding some of what people are saying about Medicine's &quot;scale&quot;, it might be helpful to think about how other abilities can have a major impact on the world first.<br /> <br /> War can dramatically reshape the direction of nations. Personal combat abilities can contribute to that, and can also be used to shut down almost any other magical power by murdering it at its source. Diplomacy and persuasion powers can change the fate of the world by altering the minds of leaders, or by (if more slowly and with more difficulty) influencing crowds and populations and so on. Even if 3e is scaling things down from the ridiculousness of Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe, I imagine that it will be quite doable to start a riot that can change the face of a city overnight.<br /> <br /> Crafting and sorcery are infrastructural powers whose scope doesn't really require any elaboration.<br /> <br /> So what about medicine? Well, in previous editions (excluding a few oddball charms) it's mostly been &quot;you can cure an important person if they happen to be sick&quot; -- which is much, much more situational (and tends to fall slightly into that 'solution looking for a problem' thing, in that even if the ST throws you a bone and gives you an important sick person to cure, you're probably going to be well-aware that this is just them deliberately creating a problem that wouldn't exist otherwise just for you to solve it -- which is never as satisfying as using words and warfare to carve your own legend on the world according to your will.)<br /> <br /> Medicine and disease are hugely important things in terms of shaping human history, but the problem that I'm seeing (based on what hatewheel is saying about the direction he's looking for above) is that most of the really major medical effects in the real world are infrastructural. Alexander Fleming and Jonas Salk may have saved more lives than even the most brutal of generals has taken, but practically speaking their advances were able to spread because of a huge and intricate social infrastructure... and if the game treats it like that, then most of the major wide-scale impact Medicine has had in the real world is outside of the reach of Medicine charms.<br /> <br /> Which is, I mean -- well, obviously &quot;cure polio&quot; and &quot;invent penicillin&quot; can't be available as one charm activation. But at the same time, when a few War and Melee guys can win a major battle, or your Zenith, Night, and Eclipse can work together to start an uprising that overthrows a major city -- the Medicine guy needs powers that <i>contribute</i>.<br /> <br /> Maybe part of this is that Medicine doesn't automatically play well with other powers. When there's a major battle, the Dawn does tactics and the Zenith and Eclipse do propaganda / morale and the Night caste assassinates enemy generals... sorcerers hit them with sorcery and anyone with information-charms (lore, investigation, awareness, etc) can get information. What does the Medicine guy do? Medicine has, up until now, been mostly calibrated at a level where it cannot contribute meaningfully to a major battle like that (yes sure you can say you're healing people and the ST will nod and this will, compared to the dramatic efforts of everyone else, accomplish exactly nothing.)<br /> <br /> Pretty much any other major task that isn't <i>directly</i> about healing the sick nobleman is going to play out exactly the same way. You want to overthrow the city government? The Night sneaks the Dawn in to murder key people, the Zenith and Eclipse do propaganda on crowds or key officials, sorcery and the things made by a crafter are still good at everything, information from Lore / Investigation is still vital, and the medicine guy... hopes someone has a sick daughter they can cure?<br /> <br /> Medicine is narrow and specific and mostly limited to small numbers of individuals and, collectively, this means it usually has very little to contribute compared to most of the other abilities. So I would tend to say that Medicine charms ought to scale up to a certain extent -- enough to influence a noticeable area in a city or a battlefield. The mechanism doesn't have to be (and shouldn't be) &quot;wave your hands and cure a bunch of people&quot;, but something like recognizing key vectors that can be used to cause or prevent outbreaks of--<br /> <br /> Bleh. You know what? Even when I put it like that, that still doesn't look like enough. Even with the broad application of Medicine where, I don't know, your medical guy figures out how to poison a well, or... keep your well from being poisoned? It's <i>still</i> a very narrow and limited contribution compared to pretty much everyone else in the scenarios I outlined. And it already feels a bit forced, in the &quot;let's find something for the medicine guy to do&quot; sense.<br /> <br /> I know that this isn't in the cards, but I am honestly, seriously wondering if maybe the game would be better without Medicine as an ability -- rolling it into Lore (yes, I know it does too much already) or Occult or Craft or something. I know there are people who enjoy focusing on it, and I'm sure it can be fun in the right game, but it is too specific and too narrow at what it does, and this is a fundamental problem with its definition, not something that can be solved by introducing clever charms.<br /> <br /> Anyway, sorry I couldn't be of more help, but I hope I at least shed some light on the issues Medicine faces and why so many people are desperately begging for a way to apply it on a larger scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T21:34:50-08:00","id":71036,"title":"","content":"Having said that, I can contribute a little bit: Rasputin managed to almost take over a government using medical knowledge. The medicine peddler from Mononoke (who used his knowledge of medicine to do things like win the trust of nobles and the like so he could carry out his mission) also comes to mind. A good doctor in a circle can be useful to build up a reputation that will give the Eclipse access to places where they wouldn't have before -- running a scheme where the Twilight Doctor takes on increasingly high-class patients and earns reputation as a miracle worker so the Eclipse and Night caste can infiltrate their families, for instance.<br /> <br /> So perhaps Medicine would benefit from charms that allow you to find things that are wrong with people at a distance (by glancing at them or even just hearing accounts), charms to help convince people to accept treatment, charms that make patients more dependent on you and which attract more patients in turn, charms that allow you to invoke your reputation and authority as a doctor...<br /> <br /> I mean, is it treading on social charms a bit? Sure. But I think there's justification. Being a good doctor (especially in a setting like this) is not simply about surgery. You need to be able to project a sense that you know what you're doing when it comes to medicine, and you need to be able to make people go along with it. The Ultimate Doctor might not be able to work a crowd like the Zenith or negotiate a treaty like the Eclipse, but they should be able to convince a noblewoman that her daughter needs treatment <i>right now</i> and that only he can cure her -- that's the kind of social authority that, I think, someone who is playing the Greatest Doctor Who Ever Lived can reasonably expect to be able to invoke without needing too much from other abilities.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think looking at Rasputin as a Twilight miracle-worker who used his capabilities as a doctor to win the trust of the royal family might help -- give Medicine charms that can actually force that situation to an extent, rather than just hoping the royal family's son is sick and that they'll <i>maybe</i> be grateful to you for saving them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-13-2014, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T22:16:59-08:00","id":71049,"title":"","content":"I don't know if someone has mentioned it, but what about Medicine Charms that declare your patients sacrosanct to forces inimical to life? Treat a patient for disease and for a time they are immune to that disease, but moreover the touch of the Solar healer smites Creatures of Darkness that attempt to poison or infect the patient.<br /> <br /> How about playing with Intimacies and healing more health levels depending on the level of Intimacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T22:47:00-08:00","id":71060,"title":"","content":"Maybe a Charm that prevents or reduces the risk of the Solar catching a disease herself? Possibly limited to when the Solar is working to heal someone of it. It wouldn't do die of the plague a day after you ride gloriously into a village to cure it, after all.<br /> <br /> Also... this isn't a specific request, and I'm not sure how it fits thematically into whatever you have planned, but I'd like the EX3 Medicine Charms to give me the option of playing both a genius super-doctor and messiah-like miracle-worker. The latter wouldn't necessarily have to be anything like being a D&amp;D Cleric - and I think I'd rather it wasn't - but... I've had ideas for characters that fit both concepts.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if there would actually need to be separate Charms supporting both concepts or not. Simply changing how you describe your character and their actions could do that, I know, but... somehow that tends to feel a bit unsatisfying to me. On the other hand, I wouldn't want a character to feel like they can't be the best doctor ever because they don't want to take the less-sciencey Charms, or vice-versa. I don't know. Fortunately, EX3 is in the hands of more talented designers than me. I just thought I should throw my thoughts out here.<br /> <br /> Sorry if any of this has already been requested. I've been a bit out of it, so I might have missed some things in reading through this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T02:33:00-08:00","id":71119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71033#post71033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many wonderful things about Medicine and scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these are great points! I don't know if getting rid of medicine completely is the best idea (or even possible at this stage) but what I take away from this is that Medicine Charms should be useful in more situations that mending a random diseased jerk, especially when the circle tackles a big problem. Something like a patch healing charm that gives a buff when that patient acts on an intimacy (possibly one given by the circle's eclipse/zenith!). A charm that turns a disability, like a magic penalty or a disease or a missing arm, into a short term bonus to combat. Drugs or treatments that calms breathing and heartbeats, allowing the patient to be sneakier as well as preserving her life.<br /> <br /> The Circle should FEEL your contribution to your goals. Medicine charms should have just as much impact and weight as combat charms. As a bit of a sketchy example, I have a 4eDND druid who's primary role in combat is to drop enemy defenses by 7 and give them vulnerabilty to damage. Debuff, debuff, debuff! My party members love to hit when they roll an unlucky 6, and their faces light up when they get to add more damage because of me. I don't do much damage myself, but when I'm not around my party's tactics and strategies change. Likewise, out of combat, I am able to sneak into places that the rest of my party can not because of my shapeshifting. Much of the time I can take them with me. Again, how my party deals with their problems changes. More brute force, less finesse. They feel it when I'm there and feel it when I'm gone.<br /> <br /> As of 2.5ed Exalted, not having someone with Medicine charms around means that they heal slower and lean heavier on defensive charms. Maybe they have to dip into resistance a bit. If somebody loses a limb, the Circle can probably go to another God or Exalt to fix the problem. A healer does not impact a Circles plans like someone who can summon demons or sneak does. Sure, they get to shine whenever a plague or poison shows up, but the ST has to go out of their way to make that happen. I would like a Medicine specialist to have as much impact on how a circle deals with their problems as the Awareness specialist, or the Melee specialist, or the Presence specialist. They should feel it when the healer is there and feel the sting when she is gone. They should branch out from just fixing injuries and curing diseases whenever it is plot appropriate and have the possibility to contribute meaningfully (but not overwhelmingly) to more situations. The Sail charms seem to have the right idea, imo.<br /> <br /> Again, not too sure how feasable this is for the core, but this is my medicine structural wish list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2258-mrstabs","name":"MrStabs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T02:46:28-08:00","id":71124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71028#post71028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However your statement of &quot;have haunted creation since day one&quot; part makes me wary, as it implies it's always been a problem and even in the first age the Solars were able to do nothing about up-scaling their powers in this field. Which now has me somewhat turned around and confused, since it would be like saying &quot;yes the solars were capable of doing great things and made great wonders to do even greater things on a larger scale, except medicine of course.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That the Solars of the First Age could develop measures to effectively deal with major problems like widespread disease does not mean that widespread disease would cease to be a concern, or that the measure against them would not require continuous maintainence and refinement.<br /> <br /> Look at real life, with the recent bird flu epidemic. A disease that could have potentially become as severe as the Spanish flu of a hundred years ago, curtailed by effective medical procedures, but ones that require significant effort to implement. We're nowhere near past the <i>existence</i> of diseases that could grow severe enough to kill millions, but, with effort and investment, we can stop them from actually doing so.<br /> <br /> Same with Solars; no Charms to say &quot;spend motes to eliminate influenza&quot; or &quot;spend motes to prevent pandemic&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, when John says he won't mechanize the solution, I imagine he means nothing like &quot;you must have this many successes on a Bureaucracy and/or Medicine roll to create worldwide pandemic response procedures&quot;, or to suggest that major response to big disease is as simple as making or finding, say, a magic cure all flower. It's as big as keeping bird flu in check, with all the story that implies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T03:30:13-08:00","id":71141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71028#post71028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However your statement of &quot;have haunted creation since day one&quot; part makes me wary, as it implies it's always been a problem and even in the first age the Solars were able to do nothing about up-scaling their powers in this field. Which now has me somewhat turned around and confused, since it would be like saying &quot;yes the solars were capable of doing great things and made great wonders to do even greater things on a larger scale, except medicine of course.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solars probably destroyed some diseases. They probably created a few nasty ones as well. And while one Solar might have eliminated all illness in his realm, that didn't help the humans the next realm over.<br /> <br /> As far as we know, the Solars weren't able to get rid of war or poverty across Creation, why is illness easier to fix than those?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T03:40:43-08:00","id":71148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71036#post71036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A great summary of medicine on the end of page 11</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with this all the way. The solar doctor needs to be an active agent in the circles story, not someone the ST has to go out of his way to incorporate. Charms that leans towards presence and socialize to make the doctor able to assert authority as The Greatest Physician and use his reputation would go a long way towards this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrStabs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71119#post71119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Comments on druid debuffing in 4eDnD</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also a way to go to make the doctor good to have in a group. Disrupting Ki Flow Strike debuff would be a good way to emulate using your expert medicinal knowledge in a combat situation and be helpful to your circlemates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T03:42:13-08:00","id":71149,"title":"","content":"I still refer to this for the Old Realm against disease:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the First Age, the Great Contagion could have been stopped cold. Leading Solar medical experts had organizations like our WHO; immortal geniuses had spent lifetimes preparing virulent outbreak contingencies, ordering the mass creation and stockpiling of medical wonders; establishing distribution networks, vaccination-firewall contingency plans, designing Charm-strengthening hospital manses for the treatment of the sick by Terrestrial doctors.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T03:52:24-08:00","id":71152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, that's why I mentioned the idea of pre-emptive life preservation. One of the great and most potent things that medicine can do is <b>keep your Exalted assets healthy and in the field</b>. But if they die, it can't do that. So instead, you prevent their death, bring back their bedraggled and shitfucked meatpile, and six-million-dollar-man it back together.<br /> <br /> The downside is I have absolutely no idea how to fit that in to the cause-and-dramatic-effect constraints.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Expand the health boxes - there's your injured health boxes, your incapacitated health boxes, your dying health boxes, your mostly dead health boxes, your really quite certainly mostly dead health boxes, and your actually dead dead health boxes.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah. Dealing with social issues, Medicine requires a specific kind of foe. As a combat-adjacent ability, it is readily useful. &quot;This is not D&amp;D, you are not a Cleric&quot; is a thing, but it really is the niche it needs to go into - combat time healing. Include limits, sure, but... without it, it's inobvious how the Doctor can be generally useful. If they're a combat asset, well, it's simpler...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T04:12:29-08:00","id":71158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71152#post71152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Expand the health boxes - there's your injured health boxes, your incapacitated health boxes, your dying health boxes, your mostly dead health boxes, your really quite certainly mostly dead health boxes, and your actually dead dead health boxes.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah. Dealing with social issues, Medicine requires a specific kind of foe. As a combat-adjacent ability, it is readily useful. &quot;This is not D&amp;D, you are not a Cleric&quot; is a thing, but it really is the niche it needs to go into - combat time healing. Include limits, sure, but... without it, it's inobvious how the Doctor can be generally useful. If they're a combat asset, well, it's simpler...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>IMO 2nd ed solar medicine had all that already<br /> <br /> Instant treatment methodology + a 2nd excellency + the 'use your essence as medicine and surgical tools' + any number of other solar medical charms are you were a walking healbot<br /> <br /> At essence 4, thanks to the errata, you can get science of mutation - which suddenly makes you the master of bad touch charms and the bane of anyone who doesn't have shaping defences: &quot;I poke him - now he can't breathe air&quot; or &quot;I poke him and now he has STR 1 and DEX 1 because all his muscles shrivel up&quot; - again you need ITM and an excellency with this.<br /> <br /> Now you're suddenly a VERY combat-capable doctor and nightmare-fuel creator.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, then charms that specifically state that they do stuff like immunization, or produce actual medicine that can be stored and distributed - that's sort of missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T04:40:26-08:00","id":71173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71026#post71026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a major problem with these kinds of effects.<br /> <br /> Here's the issue: You've basically just described a &quot;find plot&quot; charm. That is to say that the only real effect a charm like this has is to ask the ST to give you the plot. In practical terms it does nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except I never suggested the Charm do only that. The Charm could do all sorts of things to help heal fix curable diseases, just bucking up against those literally impossible to cure. Giving the plot to find how to cure the incurable is essentially a bonus investigative power that is also enabling you to do the impossible.<br /> <br /> And if I had to choose between &quot;Charm that instantly cures the incurably sick character boom no problem&quot; and &quot;Charm that doesn't but gives you the plot to do so&quot; I'd still pick the latter because at least it gives you plot, where the first one simply bypasses it.<br /> <br /> Really, you could say the same thing, &quot;it's just a find-plot charm&quot;, for any information-gathering effect.<br /> <br /> That said...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71026#post71026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't mean that your medicine charms have to be able to cure everything, of course. I'm just saying that &quot;point you in the direction of a plot device&quot; is not, itself, a meaningful power worth spending XP on; it could be a flavorful side-effect to a charm whose practical mechanical applications are elsewhere, maybe when you activate it for something it can't cure.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I meant when I posted that, with an emphasis on that I find the &quot;instant cure the incurable boom!&quot; boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T04:48:11-08:00","id":71178,"title":"","content":"I would like Ex3 Medicine to be better at healing than Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71158#post71158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At essence 4, thanks to the errata, you can get science of mutation - which suddenly makes you the master of bad touch charms and the bane of anyone who doesn't have shaping defences: &quot;I poke him - now he can't breathe air&quot; or &quot;I poke him and now he has STR 1 and DEX 1 because all his muscles shrivel up&quot; - again you need ITM and an excellency with this.<br /> <br /> Now you're suddenly a VERY combat-capable doctor and nightmare-fuel creator.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to read those Charms again.<br /> <br /> Instant Treatment Methodology only shortens Dramatic Actions that take up to an hour, and even then only down to a few seconds. Science of Mutation takes five hours. Nothing about either Charm suggests you can use them as an attack.<br /> <br /> You're a master of bad-touch effects as long as your opponent lies down and lets you perform a five hour surgical procedure.<br /> <br /> Hell, <i>I</i> could kill a guy if he let me do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 02-13-2014, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T04:48:48-08:00","id":71179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71033#post71033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much any other major task that isn't <i>directly</i> about healing the sick nobleman is going to play out exactly the same way. You want to overthrow the city government? The Night sneaks the Dawn in to murder key people, the Zenith and Eclipse do propaganda on crowds or key officials, sorcery and the things made by a crafter are still good at everything, information from Lore / Investigation is still vital, and the medicine guy... hopes someone has a sick daughter they can cure?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that could be emphasized that would make Medicine more useful is showing how, in Creation, a huge amount of the population is not healthy. They don't eat well, they don't live in good conditions. There's no hygiene. They're sick with minor ills all the damn time. Someone skilled in medicine is going to be able to simply improve the quality of life, the lifespan, the sharpness of the mind and the beauty of the body, of pretty much anybody in Creation.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how you'd build that into the system or into Solar Charms, but that's what I feel Medicine should generally enable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T06:05:42-08:00","id":71212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70956#post70956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant to quote Kunoichi earlier, in my big post, but the forum software wisely decided I was quoting someone else. Anyway, this was for you, Kunoichi:<br /> <br /> It seems many people want to be able to treat larger groups. Just remember that execution will be limited to how it pushes realism in Creation. There won't be a Charm to make your nurses just as effective as you, or a Charm to wander across a battlefield Essence-zapping people back to life. Solar Charms thrive on a logos of action and dramatic effect. This is what allows them to be so powerful. Taking away the need for logos does make them more powerful, but it also makes them into miscellaneous wish-powers, which by turns makes them uninteresting, boring, and disappointing. So my challenge here will be to make it so that you can luxuriate in the extremely difficult challenge of triage, rather than just hope your Athletics and Awareness Charms can get you where you need to go fast enough and your Medicine Excellency will help you when you get there. A large part of this is going to be on you, and the Storyteller. Making things interesting requires a little elbow grease and creative use of the system and Abilities at large. No Charm, no matter how well written, will ever suffice.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue seems to be that it's hard to separate &quot;Cure people on a large scale.&quot; (which is a very reasonable expectation for a super-doctor to do) from &quot;Press the Plague-B-Gon button, done with that plot.&quot; (which is dull and not interactive or detailed enough) Is that anywhere near right?<br /> <br /> If so, then part of the problem may be that a lot of large-scale medicine moves into the terrain of other abilities, like Lore, Craft or Bureaucracy (and historically, Sorcery). While that may be accurate, it's going to feel a bit weird if the doctor is forced to primarily use non-Medicine abilities to do their thing, and make Medicine itself feel like an afterthought for large-scale works. As a worst-case scenario, I'm imagining the sort of situation where I just need a competent mortal doctor to give me some pointers, and then use my Bureaucracy, Lore and Socialise abilities and charms to re-organise my city to eliminate serious disease outbreaks--without needing any personal medical knowledge. And the results of that are better than being the doctor in the trenches, fighting disease as if it were an invading army. Which may be quite realistic (individual medics can only do so much without social and infrastructure changes that promote better health), but it's going to make the super-healer feel a bit cheated if the Eclipse is doing more to safeguard the health of their city than the alleged medical expert can.<br /> <br /> So without knowing what exactly to do yet, I'd suggest that a large-scale Medicine charm / set of charms needs to meet these criteria:<br /> --Effective on a large scale.<br /> --Equal in &quot;wow!&quot; factor to slaughtering an army or converting a city, and not significantly more difficult than those things.<br /> --Unquestionably better at healing or prevention than what other abilities can do.<br /> --Interactive, requiring choices, tactical use and decisions other than &quot;activate power&quot;.<br /> <br /> Does that sound right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","user":"Elemental","date":". 02-13-2014, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T06:27:05-08:00","id":71221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70956#post70956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems many people want to be able to treat larger groups. Just remember that execution will be limited to how it pushes realism in Creation. There won't be a Charm to make your nurses just as effective as you, or a Charm to wander across a battlefield Essence-zapping people back to life. Solar Charms thrive on a logos of action and dramatic effect. This is what allows them to be so powerful. Taking away the need for logos does make them more powerful, but it also makes them into miscellaneous wish-powers, which by turns makes them uninteresting, boring, and disappointing. So my challenge here will be to make it so that you can luxuriate in the extremely difficult challenge of triage, rather than just hope your Athletics and Awareness Charms can get you where you need to go fast enough and your Medicine Excellency will help you when you get there. A large part of this is going to be on you, and the Storyteller. Making things interesting requires a little elbow grease and creative use of the system and Abilities at large. No Charm, no matter how well written, will ever suffice.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this topic, a Charm that could meaningfully enhance triage or sustained, fast-pace treatment of large groups while preserving drama and realism might be something like a toned-down, more situational Infinite Medicine Mastery. Like, you'd need a large corps of stretcher-jockeys and nurses keeping you supplied with a steady stream of tools, medicines, and the wounded, but when your Solar battlefield doctor is in Crisis Mode they could, for example, use Charms that would ordinarily enhance only a single test to instead enhance extended/dramatic actions to provide that treatment many times within a single scene, or recoup some of their spent Essence after an unsuccessful attempt to save a patient as they're filled with renewed determination not to let the next one go, or something of that nature. I think that would be cool, and turn the impossible into the merely grueling in a very satisfying and dramatic sort of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":1821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","user":"Golden Demon","date":". 02-13-2014, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T07:07:02-08:00","id":71252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71212#post71212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, then part of the problem may be that a lot of large-scale medicine moves into the terrain of other abilities, like Lore, Craft or Bureaucracy (and historically, Sorcery). While that may be accurate, it's going to feel a bit weird if the doctor is forced to primarily use non-Medicine abilities to do their thing, and make Medicine itself feel like an afterthought for large-scale works. As a worst-case scenario, I'm imagining the sort of situation where I just need a competent mortal doctor to give me some pointers, and then use my Bureaucracy, Lore and Socialise abilities and charms to re-organise my city to eliminate serious disease outbreaks--without needing any personal medical knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm. Is it bad if a warrior needs War to do large scale combat? Or an investigator a team (and effectively leading that team requiring Socialize or Presence or whatev) to do large scale policing? Or a crafter a labor force (run with Bureaucracy) to do large-scale building? I think this may come back to the reason (1) Twilights have Lore, Craft, and their other abilities; to affectively apply small scale stuff like medicine on a larger scale. Same reason Dawns have War. And (2) the reason a Solar works with other Solars. Plus I'm pretty sure a mortal doctor giving pointers wouldn't really be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:01:32-08:00","id":71300,"title":"","content":"The Socialize preview Charms kind of do that already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:03:21-08:00","id":71305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading a book titled <i>The Spirit Catches You And You Fall Down</i>, which is about the doctors in the california town of Merced trying to provide medical care to a Hmong family with a daughter prone to grand mal seizures. The hmong family is illiterate and does not believe in western medicine and in fact intermittently suspects that the fevers and illnesses their daughter suffers are the fault of the medications she has been prescribed - that the doctors are intentionally making her ill. It is a very large cultural and language barrier that prevents proper care from being administered.<br /> <br /> A Solar doctor should be able to punch through that sort of confusion like a bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally A Doctor Prana, go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:34:28-08:00","id":71330,"title":"","content":"Okay, everything Aquillion has said in this thread has been basically exactly true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:37:50-08:00","id":71331,"title":"","content":"Can there be a charm where people trust you when you are going to perform an operation/surgery of some kind?<br /> Trust me, I'm a doctor Prana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:42:31-08:00","id":71338,"title":"","content":"And for when Medicine overlaps with other Abilities, you have Dammit Jim, I'm a Doctor Prana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:58:35-08:00","id":71352,"title":"","content":"So if your character want to know if the wound on the corpse body was caused by some sharp instrument or not, do you use Investigation, Lore or Medicine. Or more specifically, what ability does forensic fall in to. On one hand, poking corpse with a stick will require medical knowledge (Lore ? Medicine ?). On the other hand, Investigation <i>is </i>the detective ability so.............","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T09:13:26-08:00","id":71369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71352#post71352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if your character want to know if the wound on the corpse body was caused by some sharp instrument or not, do you use Investigation, Lore or Medicine. Or more specifically, what ability does forensic fall in to. On one hand, poking corpse with a stick will require medical knowledge (Lore ? Medicine ?). On the other hand, Investigation <i>is </i>the detective ability so.............</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always run it that a basic examination of a dead body can be done with Investigation, while a deeper probing requires Medicine. It's the difference between being Sherlock and being Watson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T09:17:18-08:00","id":71372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71352#post71352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if your character want to<b> know if the wound on the corpse body was caused by some sharp instrument or not</b>, do you use Investigation, Lore or Medicine. Or more specifically, what ability does forensic fall in to. On one hand, poking corpse with a stick will require medical knowledge (Lore ? Medicine ?). On the other hand, Investigation <i>is </i>the detective ability so.............</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably wouldn't use anything. Unless 3e is going very far away and having you roll everything you don't roll dice for simple/obvious things.<br /> <br /> Now something like &quot;Which of these 237 open wounds on the body is the one that killed them&quot; would be medicine.<br /> &quot;How did this person get 237 open wounds and then die of an exploded and untouched heart?&quot; would be investigation<br /> &quot;What is capable of inflicting this many open wounds and exploding hearts?&quot; would be lore or possibly occult.<br /> &quot;Why did Butcher B'zhal return to the area and why did he turn this person into a connect the dots message reading 'Hero! I have returned, prepare to face your inevitable decent into madness and doom', and how did they get the message that compact?&quot; is the story setup and possibly a linguistics challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T09:51:29-08:00","id":71390,"title":"","content":"What about a charm that let you proscribe a general remedy for something which other people, even mortal, could use? Like telling all the lepers to go wash in the Grey River or writing a formula of rose lozenge that cures the common cold that anyone with the write training could make. There would have to be some limit, like only while you committed essence or only in a very small geographic area. Perhaps an upgrade could make them permanent so suddenly, roses from Zarlath help fight off the cold or bark of the Aspra tree cures headaches.<br /> <br /> Also, assuming there isn't some form of CNNT type total replacement, there could be a charm that lets you use unconventional material for treatment. Mud instead of salve, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T10:20:41-08:00","id":71409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71252#post71252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm. Is it bad if a warrior needs War to do large scale combat? Or an investigator a team (and effectively leading that team requiring Socialize or Presence or whatev) to do large scale policing? Or a crafter a labor force (run with Bureaucracy) to do large-scale building? I think this may come back to the reason (1) Twilights have Lore, Craft, and their other abilities; to affectively apply small scale stuff like medicine on a larger scale. Same reason Dawns have War. And (2) the reason a Solar works with other Solars. Plus I'm pretty sure a mortal doctor giving pointers wouldn't really be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But the difference is, the effect of tactical planning is to make the actual combat more effective, and the social rolls make the investigation more effective. They don't (and shouldn't) edge Melee or Craft out of their supposed specialties, which seems to be the problem with Medicine being overshadowed.<br /> <br /> It keeps coming back to this--if someone goes with &quot;legendary healer&quot; as their concept, and wants to cure a city of a plague, they shouldn't be told &quot;Well, you should have bought social / crafting skills if you want to do anything for more than a few dozen people.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T10:23:45-08:00","id":71410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrStabs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71119#post71119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of 2.5ed Exalted, not having someone with Medicine charms around means that they heal slower and lean heavier on defensive charms. Maybe they have to dip into resistance a bit. If somebody loses a limb, the Circle can probably go to another God or Exalt to fix the problem. A healer does not impact a Circles plans like someone who can summon demons or sneak does. Sure, they get to shine whenever a plague or poison shows up, but the ST has to go out of their way to make that happen. I would like a Medicine specialist to have as much impact on how a circle deals with their problems as the Awareness specialist, or the Melee specialist, or the Presence specialist. They should feel it when the healer is there and feel the sting when she is gone. They should branch out from just fixing injuries and curing diseases whenever it is plot appropriate and have the possibility to contribute meaningfully (but not overwhelmingly) to more situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with &quot;focus on how much the circle needs you&quot; is that then you end up with the D&amp;D cleric problem, where you have the group designing their characters and someone says &quot;all right, one of us has to bite the bullet and take Medicine&quot; and everyone groans and he's like &quot;yes, but you all know how much the game sucks without it&quot; and finally someone says &quot;FINE, I'll do it but you owe me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem isn't that Medicine isn't necessary; the problem is that it isn't <i>fun</i> -- it usually gives you fewer options to contribute compared to other powers, and when you do contribute, it often feels like a mindless healbot thing where you repair problems outside of combat when it would be obvious for you to repair them, with little room for creative use of your abilities. Making Medicine more essential without making it more fun (and giving it more applicability) would make things worse, because now you'd be forcing people who aren't even interested in it in the first place to take it just to make the game fun for everyone else. Or, to put it in simpler terms, you want to avoid deliberately punishing the rest of the circle because their Twilight <i>didn't</i> take medicine, because that sets up a very unfun dynamic for everyone involved.<br /> <br /> In other words: The game needs to be entirely playable with nobody in the circle who has Medicine charms. Making Medicine essential isn't really solving the issue -- you don't want to force people to use Medicine, you want them to enjoy it. And in general, I think what people enjoy about their powers is when they're able to use them in interesting and creative ways, not when they do the mandatory healbot thing every time the Dawn gets a crippling effect from a nasty fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-13-2014, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T10:33:44-08:00","id":71416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71410#post71410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with &quot;focus on how much the circle needs you&quot; is that then you end up with the D&amp;D cleric problem, where you have the group designing their characters and someone says &quot;all right, one of us has to bite the bullet and take Medicine&quot; and everyone groans and he's like &quot;yes, but you all know how much the game sucks without it&quot; and finally someone says &quot;FINE, I'll do it but you owe me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem isn't that Medicine isn't necessary; the problem is that it isn't <i>fun</i> -- it usually gives you fewer options to contribute compared to other powers, and when you do contribute, it often feels like a mindless healbot thing where you repair problems outside of combat when it would be obvious for you to repair them, with little room for creative use of your abilities. Making Medicine more essential without making it more fun (and giving it more applicability) would make things worse, because now you'd be forcing people who aren't even interested in it in the first place to take it just to make the game fun for everyone else. Or, to put it in simpler terms, you want to avoid deliberately punishing the rest of the circle because their Twilight <i>didn't</i> take medicine, because that sets up a very unfun dynamic for everyone involved.<br /> <br /> In other words: The game needs to be entirely playable with nobody in the circle who has Medicine charms. Making Medicine essential isn't really solving the issue -- you don't want to force people to use Medicine, you want them to enjoy it. And in general, I think what people enjoy about their powers is when they're able to use them in interesting and creative ways, not when they do the mandatory healbot thing every time the Dawn gets a crippling effect from a nasty fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the best way to deal with this is to step out of the D&amp;D paradigm and give people something to DO - most D&amp;D games don't focus on curing somebody of cancer and then observing the joy you have brought them, or repairing a community ravaged by leprosy. For my table at least, the rewards of these actions may be primarily emotional or story-based, but they are still 'carrots' that are sought eagerly by my players.<br /> <br /> Medicine allows you to make the harsh reality of the world slightly less stinging, which depending on the plot you put forward, may end up being the most important power in the world to your players.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D doesn't emphasise these social issues as much, so of course the ability to heal is therefore significantly devalued. Viewed through the lens of combat utility, possibly the most miraculous and awesome supernatural power people could GET is actually kinda boring!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:23:23-08:00","id":71456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading a book titled <i>The Spirit Catches You And You Fall Down</i>, which is about the doctors in the california town of Merced trying to provide medical care to a Hmong family with a daughter prone to grand mal seizures. The hmong family is illiterate and does not believe in western medicine and in fact intermittently suspects that the fevers and illnesses their daughter suffers are the fault of the medications she has been prescribed - that the doctors are intentionally making her ill. It is a very large cultural and language barrier that prevents proper care from being administered.<br /> <br /> A Solar doctor should be able to punch through that sort of confusion like a bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">IIRC, the really awful thing is that while the parents were wrong about the doctors intentionally making her ill, they're weren't neccessarily wrong about the medicine making things worse. It's just that it was impossible for them to convey this to the doctors in a way that the doctors wouldn't dismiss in a well-meaning fashion.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you want more detail on cross-cultural stuff, I found Arthur Kleinman's <i>Rethinking Psychiatry</i>, which looks at cross cultural issues in mental health, to be very interesting. (Kleinman is at one point consulted by the author of <i>The Spirit Catches You</i> in order to find out what one should do when dealing with complicated cross cultural medical issues.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:32:50-08:00","id":71467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading a book titled <i>The Spirit Catches You And You Fall Down</i>, which is about the doctors in the california town of Merced trying to provide medical care to a Hmong family with a daughter prone to grand mal seizures. The hmong family is illiterate and does not believe in western medicine and in fact intermittently suspects that the fevers and illnesses their daughter suffers are the fault of the medications she has been prescribed - that the doctors are intentionally making her ill. It is a very large cultural and language barrier that prevents proper care from being administered.<br /> <br /> A Solar doctor should be able to punch through that sort of confusion like a bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, that's easy. A perfect bedside manner charm. Some of the more impressive benefits could be - making it hard for people to freak out or take negative conditions, being able to help people stay in one place for a long period of time and not go crazy, and perhaps most important - being able to explain treatment and treatment options in a 'culturally sensitive way' that somehow manages to communicate the essential information even if you dance around for a while waving sticks explaining how the Ooga Booga interacts with the Splin-Splarn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:18:40-08:00","id":71506,"title":"","content":"I dunno about social Charms in Medicine.<br /> <br /> If a Solar doctor really wants that edge, there's several entire trees for it. Pick up a little Socialize or Presence and you're good to go.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I also think that the doctor who has miraculous healing abilities but still has to deal with exactly the kind of distrust Kukla is relating could be a viable and interesting Exalted concept. Sure, they could just not take that Charm, but if you want to be the Ultimate Doctor <i>and</i> have superhuman bedside manner, I don't think it's unreasonable to expect a small dip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:27:58-08:00","id":71514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71506#post71506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno about social Charms in Medicine. If a Solar doctor really wants that edge, there's several entire trees for it. Pick up a little Socialize or Presence and you're good to go. On the other hand, I also think that the doctor who has miraculous healing abilities but still has to deal with exactly the kind of distrust Kukla is relating could be a viable and interesting Exalted concept. Sure, they could just not take that Charm, but if you want to be the Ultimate Doctor <i>and</i> have superhuman bedside manner, I don't think it's unreasonable to expect a small dip.</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on how unsurpassed that manner is. A salty dog method type thing would work, being able to convince all the denizens of the imperial city to come to your tanning salon/hospital does not belong in medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:38:21-08:00","id":71521,"title":"","content":"I do think that a Solar doctor who has to prove himself in a distrusting environment should have the same obstacle to overcome as a Solar warrior who has to. You can use your social skills to win them over or you can cure the local plague/fight off the local bandits to achieve that result. Just because doctors &amp; medicines aren't trusted doesn't mean Medicine Charms should offer the power to directly overcome that. Some level of overlap between Abilities and their Charms is one thing, but I think it's a bit too much for there to be a Bedside Manner Prana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:11:15-08:00","id":71551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70422#post70422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Solar physician bring someone back from the dead? Nope. Dead is dead.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't want D&amp;D Resurrection, but solar Medicine should at least equal modern real world Medicine in regards to how far gone you can be and still be pulled back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:17:14-08:00","id":71560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71551#post71551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wouldn't want D&amp;D Resurrection, but solar Medicine should at least equal modern real world Medicine in regards to how far gone you can be and still be pulled back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that plays into what John said about a distinction between narrative death (which is absolute and cannot be undone) and mechanical death (which can be worked around with &quot;I got his heart going again!&quot; or &quot;it was a death-like trance the whole time&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:21:21-08:00","id":71564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71521#post71521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that a Solar doctor who has to prove himself in a distrusting environment should have the same obstacle to overcome as a Solar warrior who has to. You can use your social skills to win them over or you can cure the local plague/fight off the local bandits to achieve that result. Just because doctors &amp; medicines aren't trusted doesn't mean Medicine Charms should offer the power to directly overcome that. Some level of overlap between Abilities and their Charms is one thing, but I think it's a bit too much for there to be a Bedside Manner Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71560#post71560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that plays into what John said about a distinction between narrative death (which is absolute and cannot be undone) and mechanical death (which can be worked around with &quot;I got his heart going again!&quot; or &quot;it was a death-like trance the whole time&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Mechanical death can fuel drama. The drama of trying to resuscitate a person is always good. A narrative death is the only one you can't come back from. Mechanical death can become narrative death if there's no way of reversing it, such as a person getting beheaded or disintegrated, or just dying hours before a Solar can get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:26:13-08:00","id":71568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71564#post71564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Mechanical death can fuel drama. The drama of trying to resuscitate a person is always good. A narrative death is the only one you can't come back from. Mechanical death can become narrative death if there's no way of reversing it, such as a person getting beheaded or disintegrated, or just dying hours before a Solar can get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most solidly. The whole fighting death against terrible odds was one of the big themes in the old MASH movie/TV Show. It resonates with people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:42:28-08:00","id":71575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71564#post71564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. Mechanical death can fuel drama. The drama of trying to resuscitate a person is always good. A narrative death is the only one you can't come back from. Mechanical death can become narrative death if there's no way of reversing it, such as a person getting <u><b>beheaded</b></u> or disintegrated, or just dying hours before a Solar can get there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given that <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Head_transplant\" target=\"_blank\">head transplants</a> (Don't read about this; you've been warned) on animals have been around for over 50 years, I think it's not unreasonable that Solar medicine should be able to reattach a head, if they act quickly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:49:52-08:00","id":71582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71575#post71575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Given that <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Head_transplant\" target=\"_blank\">head transplants</a> (Don't read about this; you've been warned) on animals have been around for over 50 years, I think it's not unreasonable that Solar medicine should be able to reattach a head, if they act quickly!</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, they <i>do</i> say that the head is alive for 20-30 seconds, so there's some logic to this.<br /> <br /> On the other, beheading is such a classic &quot;make sure it's dead&quot; move that I'm not sure I am okay with anyone coming back from that - unless it's being used to show how inhuman they are, anyway.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20130210183959/jjba/images/0/08/Dioheadstab.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> P.S. Dio Brando is the <i>best</i> Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:52:54-08:00","id":71587,"title":"","content":"Having burning daiclave that cauterizes the wound is now a thing, to prevent those pesky regenerating Anathema from reattaching their heads","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:17:21-08:00","id":71610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71582#post71582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the one hand, they <i>do</i> say that the head is alive for 20-30 seconds, so there's some logic to this.<br /> <br /> On the other, beheading is such a classic &quot;make sure it's dead&quot; move that I'm not sure I am okay with anyone coming back from that - unless it's being used to show how inhuman they are, anyway.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20130210183959/jjba/images/0/08/Dioheadstab.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> P.S. Dio Brando is the <i>best</i> Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>First thing that jumps to mind, Gemma from Ninja Scroll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:21:39-08:00","id":71612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that the Exalted don't bleed to death, get infections in their wounds, or die of mundane diseases,</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be incorrect. Bleeding wounds on an Exalted are closed and staunched with trivial ease but you still need to take action to do so. However most games I've been in ignore this. By the same note, they're exceptionally hardy with bonuses to resist disease and infection, but they can still die of them, even the mundane variety. They don't have a lot to fear because frankly you really have to screw up as an exalt to die from such things, but it's still there. Again, every game I've seen ignores it because the 2e disease rules are less than ideal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:32:33-08:00","id":71620,"title":"","content":"It is, however, an endorsement for greater ability to revive &quot;mechanically dead&quot; Exalts who got impaled or what have you, so that's neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:40:57-08:00","id":71628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71416#post71416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the best way to deal with this is to step out of the D&amp;D paradigm and give people something to DO - most D&amp;D games don't focus on curing somebody of cancer and then observing the joy you have brought them, or repairing a community ravaged by leprosy. For my table at least, the rewards of these actions may be primarily emotional or story-based, but they are still 'carrots' that are sought eagerly by my players.<br /> <br /> Medicine allows you to make the harsh reality of the world slightly less stinging, which depending on the plot you put forward, may end up being the most important power in the world to your players.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D doesn't emphasise these social issues as much, so of course the ability to heal is therefore significantly devalued. Viewed through the lens of combat utility, possibly the most miraculous and awesome supernatural power people could GET is actually kinda boring!</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistically, previous editions of medicine (again, barring a few admittedly-oddball DotFA charms we've been specifically told are not coming back) have not given you any tools that would help you approach a large community ravaged by leprosy. I don't mean that it's weak, I mean that you can functionally do nothing beyond maybe cure a handful of people a day as an inspiration -- which is cool, but will have no practical effect whatsoever on the larger problem.<br /> <br /> A typical Zenith or Eclipse caste, with no Medicine whatsoever (or maybe just a few dots to give them a general idea of what usually works), is going to be vastly better at handling a major disease outbreak than a dedicated corebook Solar doctor -- even if they have no idea what the appropriate medical approach is, their charms will help them ensure that the sick are quarantined and cared for, and allow them to encourage and implement systems that can provide better nutrition and sanitation. No corebook Medicine charm will help in that situation at all.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can throw the player a bone by giving them a small number of important sick people to heal, or just let them use their power like a drop in the bucket and gloss over the fact that they're accomplishing almost nothing (beyond maybe a small morale boost, which the Zenith would be vastly better at). And some players are probably perfectly willing to suspend their disbelief, activate their medicine charms on a handful of people, and go home feeling like they made a difference. But when it comes to confronting the problems most circles naturally tend to focus on -- <i>even including medical problems</i> -- you would be much better served with charms from other trees. And -- in my experience -- most players are happier when they have powerful, general-purpose tools that let them decide overarching goals and work towards attaining them. Social charms do that. Combat charms do that. Sorcery does that. Crafting and infrastructural charms do that. Medicine doesn't. They can solve that one specific sort of problem if you, as the ST, hand it to them; but they tend to not have much applicability for anything else.<br /> <br /> (This leads to the situation where Presence, Performance, Bureaucracy, and Socialize charms -- backed up with maybe a few dots of medicine to tell you how to use them, at best -- are vastly better for dealing with large-scale disease outbreaks than Medicine charms, because social charms are flexible and versatile. I can come up with a complicated, clever plan and use social charms to implement it; with Medicine, I'm generally limited to one tightly-boxed effect which does one specific thing, and my charms provide no real assistance when I want to do anything beyond that.)<br /> <br /> Keep in mind I'm not talking about huge sweeping things like 2e Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe here. Even at very basic things like &quot;save a small town from the plague&quot;, Medicine is ineffectual compared to things like Presence, Performance, Socialize -- honestly, nearly any non-combat ability beyond Ride or Sail (which have similar issues) would be better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-13-2014, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:46:29-08:00","id":71631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71628#post71628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind I'm not talking about huge sweeping things like 2e Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe here. Even at very basic things like &quot;save a small town from the plague&quot;, Medicine is ineffectual compared to things like Presence, Performance, Socialize -- honestly, nearly any non-combat ability beyond Ride or Sail (which have similar issues) would be better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aquillion: saying things better than I did since (at least) Nov 2013.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:51:36-08:00","id":71635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71612#post71612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be incorrect. Bleeding wounds on an Exalted are closed and staunched with trivial ease but you still need to take action to do so. However most games I've been in ignore this. By the same note, they're exceptionally hardy with bonuses to resist disease and infection, but they can still die of them, even the mundane variety. They don't have a lot to fear because frankly you really have to screw up as an exalt to die from such things, but it's still there. Again, every game I've seen ignores it because the 2e disease rules are less than ideal.</div> </div> </div> </div>UGH bleeding rules. Exalted can close their wounds with a reflexive diff 2 Stam + Resist roll on any action tick. Outside of combat, anyone with Medicine 1+ can close an Exalt's wound by taking an action.<br /> <br /> Mortals have it worse. To close a wound someone has to make a Wits + Medicine roll at a diff of the number of hls damage associated with the wound. If not staunched, they take an unsoakable lhl per Stam minutes.<br /> <br /> (I hope Ex3 has easier-to-use rules for bleeding.)<br /> <br /> Exalted can also get infection from wounds! Exalted probably only once since the wound closes so quickly. Morbidity is always 1 instead of ever-rising, and Virulence is at -2 (so normally 1 or 2). And like most diseases, Exalted only get symptoms (ie penalties) and won't ever die from it.<br /> <br /> (I hope Exalted has better rules for diseases.)<br /> <br /> Only in one game have I ever used these rules for Exalted. Just like most games I've played never use the generic rules for inflicting knockback of stunning, and how almost no game I've played has ever applied a circumstantial penalty to a social roll.<br /> <br /> <i>anyway</i>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71409#post71409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. But the difference is, the effect of tactical planning is to make the actual combat more effective, and the social rolls make the investigation more effective. They don't (and shouldn't) edge Melee or Craft out of their supposed specialties, which seems to be the problem with Medicine being overshadowed.<br /> <br /> It keeps coming back to this--if someone goes with &quot;legendary healer&quot; as their concept, and wants to cure a city of a plague, they shouldn't be told &quot;Well, you should have bought social / crafting skills if you want to do anything for more than a few dozen people.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed my point. For example, the character with &quot;legendary warrior&quot; as a concept still is told &quot;well you should've gotten War if you want to fight more than a few dozen people at a go.&quot; The &quot;legendary investigator&quot; is told &quot;well you need social Abilities if you want to carry on more than a few investigations at a time. The &quot;legendary crafter&quot; is told &quot;well you need Bureaucracy if you want to do anything more than hand-made crafts and not take forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> By the same token, as the warrior or crafter are not edged out of their supposed specialties by having other Abilities that extend the scope of their powers, nor should the medic be overshadowed by requiring other Abilities to extend the scope of their powers.<br /> <br /> Game design can really go either way: you can fill an Ability with Charms that cover pretty much everything someone of that archetype would want to do, or limit it so such characters would have to dip into other Ability trees. Some Abilities (the ones that are significantly limited in some way, like Sail) could have more of the former while other Abilites (that are more ubiquitous) could be more the latter. It's not a bad thing to encourage cross-Ability synergies, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:54:54-08:00","id":71636,"title":"","content":"I should add -- of course, if your group is trying to save a town from the plague, ideally everyone should contribute. It's not really a combat task, but having the medicine guy use charms to produce special citywide procedures which the Zenith and Eclipse then convince people to implement would be cool. So there's room for interesting charms and interactions between abilities there.<br /> <br /> But even if you allow that, medicine still hits a brick wall whenever you're trying to deal with something that isn't specifically and obviously a &quot;medicine problem&quot;. No ability is omni-applicable, but it is <i>much</i> easier for a Melee guy or a Presence guy to find a way to apply their abilities in typical tasks than it is for the Medicine guy -- even in the non-combat task I outlined above, say, it's still very very useful to have the Invincible Sword Princess or Killfuck Soulshitter standing behind you glowering and making sure nobody gets ideas while you convince people to do what you say.<br /> <br /> So what I'd like most out of Medicine charms, I guess, is some degree of powers with broad applicability, or things that let me say &quot;alright, I'm going to approach this with my medical knowledge&quot; even in situations where it isn't immediately obvious that that's the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:05:12-08:00","id":71645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71612#post71612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be incorrect. Bleeding wounds on an Exalted are closed and staunched with trivial ease but you still need to take action to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div> Obviously, I can't speak for 3rd Edition, but regarding 2nd Edition, your point is technically correct, but practically irrelevant:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Reflexive Actions</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some actions are reflexive, meaning <b><u>they do not require any deliberate attention from the character to perform</u></b>, nor do they cause or suffer from multiple-action penalties. If a character approaches an ambush, his player could certainly make regular (Perception + Awareness) rolls if the character was feeling paranoid. However, even if the character is not actively looking out for an ambush, he might notice the glint of moonlight on a crouched assassin\u2019s knife with just enough time to shout a warning and respond. The latter sort of check would be reflexive. Resisting poison and disease also count as reflexive actions (as do any action where the character has an innate defense that is rolled, rather than modifying the difficulty of a roll as most defenses do). Of particular note, the activation of a reflexive type Charm is always a reflexive action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stopping Bleeding is reflexive, it doesn't require any deliberate attention from the character to perform.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Bleeding:</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters suffering from lethal or aggravated damage continue to deteriorate as a result of hemorrhaging until they stanch their wounds. <u><b>Exalted and beings of similar resilience may draw their wounds closed with a successful reflexive (Stamina + Resistance) roll (difficulty 2)</b></u> on the part of their players, and they may attempt this feat in combat on any tick in which they may act. Outside of combat, characters can try this every five seconds. Furthermore, bleeding stops as soon as anyone with Medicine 1+ takes an action to treat the wounds<br /> Mortals are not so lucky as the Chosen. Stanching a wound requires a successful (Wits + Medicine) roll at a difficulty equal to the number of lethal or aggravated health levels associated with that injury. This is a standard miscellaneous action in combat. For instance, a character who was stabbed twice in the belly for two and then three level health levels would need to succeed at two separate stanching attempts, one at difficulty 2 and one at 3, respectively. Stanching requires bandaging materials, but these materials can be improvised under duress from any torn strip of cloth. Any strenuous activity, including combat and anything requiring Athletics rolls, will reopen a mortal\u2019s stanched wounds, but the Exalted and other magical beings with an innate lethal soak are immune to the dangers of reopened wounds. As long as a character suffers from bleeding wounds, she suffers one level of unsoakable lethal damage every increment of (Stamina) minutes. Mortals who do not receive prompt medical attention can and will bleed to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're an exalt. You have Stamina 2 and Resistance 0. You will bleed every 120 ticks (2 minutes). You can reflexively roll 2 dice (Stamina 2 and Resistance 0) with a difficulty of 2 to stop this. You have to fail 23 rolls for this to happen (120/5 = 24, but I assume you need to have succeeded before the 2 minutes are up, at 1 minute 55 seconds). With 2 dice you have a 72% chance of failure. The chance of failing 23 times is .72^23 = 0.0523175524% about 1 time in 1,911.<br /> <br /> If you actually have some Resistance or even more effective Stamina 3? Not happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71612#post71612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However most games I've been in ignore this.</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably because there's virtually no chance of it actually happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":299,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","user":"NineDaysDead","date":". 02-13-2014, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:08:03-08:00","id":71648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71564#post71564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Mechanical death can fuel drama. The drama of trying to resuscitate a person is always good. A narrative death is the only one you can't come back from. Mechanical death can become narrative death if there's no way of reversing it, such as a person getting beheaded or disintegrated, or just dying hours before a Solar can get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, something to provide for my need to have a Green Sun Prince vapourise Tepet Ejava's lower body with Green Sun Nimbus Flare and have it be possible for her to be kept alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T16:02:13-08:00","id":71684,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there's some room for overlap with bureaucracy and craft - cures through fixing inauspicious essence flow in systems as if they were diseases in people? Working it's way thematically from &quot;knowing that living next to a garbage dump is pretty bad for you&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/855-magistrate","name":"Magistrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T16:11:29-08:00","id":71689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71648#post71648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally, something to provide for my need to have a Green Sun Prince vapourise Tepet Ejava's lower body with Green Sun Nimbus Flare and have it be possible for her to be kept alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>...that is disturbingly specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T16:30:49-08:00","id":71704,"title":"","content":"I want to be able to heal a stab wound with a punch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T16:47:45-08:00","id":71715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71636#post71636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even if you allow that, medicine still hits a brick wall whenever you're trying to deal with something that isn't specifically and obviously a &quot;medicine problem&quot;. No ability is omni-applicable, but it is <i>much</i> easier for a Melee guy or a Presence guy to find a way to apply their abilities in typical tasks than it is for the Medicine guy -- even in the non-combat task I outlined above, say, it's still very very useful to have the Invincible Sword Princess or Killfuck Soulshitter standing behind you glowering and making sure nobody gets ideas while you convince people to do what you say.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely true from my experiences. While not as bad as, say, Sail or Ride, Medicine is definitely closer to those in terms of general applicability than it is, say, Presence or Resistance. So...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71636#post71636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what I'd like most out of Medicine charms, I guess, is some degree of powers with broad applicability, or things that let me say &quot;alright, I'm going to approach this with my medical knowledge&quot; even in situations where it isn't immediately obvious that that's the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much agree with this. Charms along the lines of Salty Dog Method where you can apply medical knowledge to things possibly outside of direct medicine would definitely be a boon to characters that focus in it getting more use out of it. I'm not entirely sure how broad Medicine should go, though, as that depends on a lot of other factors we're obviously not seeing yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T17:17:49-08:00","id":71731,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that a Solar who wants to treat a bunch of mortals with his Charms in a short frame of time should have a relatively cheap Charm that only prevents someone from dying, no matter how horrible their injuries.<br /> <br /> So he can treat a plague through a combination of this Charm, quarantining the victims to prevent the disease from spreading any further, and then spending anywhere from a week to a month using his more expensive Charms to bring each individual back to full health.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unless the new Battlegroup rules are similar to Mass Combat, in which a Solar Melee expert can use his expensive Melee Charms and Combos to kill hundreds of dudes with singular attacks. Because then I'd wonder if large numbers of sick people could be treated as a Battlegroup for healing purposes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T18:04:48-08:00","id":71757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71731#post71731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the new Battlegroup rules are similar to Mass Combat, in which a Solar Melee expert can use his expensive Melee Charms and Combos to kill hundreds of dudes with singular attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the system's changed quite a bit, this seems possible, but may not always be applicable (&quot;in some circumstances&quot;).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: (AliphanG)</b><br /> <i>I'm curious, Holden: how important do you feel &quot;morale&quot;, in the D&amp;D sense, is to Exalted 3E burly-brawls? Is it mostly confined to magickal effects, is Legion of Silence Guy so terrifying that the last 900 bandits scatter after he kills the first 100, or what?</i><br /> <br /> A: <b>(Holden)</b><br /> It's baked in to the point where damage to a battle group is considered to consist partly of incapacitated/dead opponents and partly of people losing their nerve and no longer contributing meaningfully to the fight, and defeating a BG is usually achieved through rout. There's a &quot;slaughter&quot; action you can take in some circumstances to just wreak massive carnage on a defeated BG that is lighting the hell out of there.<br /> <br /> The traditional Abyssal zombie army is scary because you can't break it-- you have to beat your way through it until they're all dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if what applies to direct combat Abilities should necessarily apply to other Abilities like this. Not that I have a horse in this race: so long as it's balanced by whatever reasonable, decided standard and someone can potentially mainline Medicine alone (like Holden's example of someone building around Awareness), I should be happy with whatever we get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T00:46:01-08:00","id":71859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71689#post71689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...that is disturbingly specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you ever see Source Code? The image comes from what turns out to be the extent of somebody's injuries.<br /> <br /> It's Ejava because I think she's badass enough to take something like that and live.<br /> <br /> Also she then gets to have a cool prosthetic lower body of green jade!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:36:36-08:00","id":71894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71859#post71859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Did you ever see Source Code? The image comes from what turns out to be the extent of somebody's injuries. It's Ejava because I think she's badass enough to take something like that and live. Also she then gets to have a cool prosthetic lower body of green jade!</div> </div> </div> </div> But....but why? Just to seriously piss her off and then troll face out of there? Or is it to get her off your back so you can slay the red piss legion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:48:37-08:00","id":71901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71894#post71894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But....but why? Just to seriously piss her off and then troll face out of there? Or is it to get her off your back so you can slay the red piss legion?</div> </div> </div> </div>To... to kill her.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously it doesn't work. Either because somebody manages to get her away from that battle with all due haste, or else the Infernal then walks away because they assume, not unreasonably, that such a wound is mortal.<br /> <br /> Okay, the greater point is that I'd like mechanical death and the capacity to be revived from it to provide an opportunity for narratives where a character is wounded to the most extreme degree imaginable and then left for dead or rapidly pulled out of the battle because somebody who wants them alive can see that this is at its worst, and the character can then come back from that.<br /> <br /> I just like framing such things in terms of specific narratives, and that one appeals to me because the Roseblack is worthy of a badass green jade lower body prosthetic, and Green Sun Princes have Charms to shoot toxic fire, God knows they <i>should</i> be disintegrating large portions of people's bodies.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a more palatable example.<br /> <br /> Spoilers for the season 2 finale of Avatar: the Last Airbender.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I want a scene like Aang being shot in the spine with lightning, and then it being possible to return him from the brink with sacred medicine.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T06:15:52-08:00","id":71937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71648#post71648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally, something to provide for my need to have a Green Sun Prince vapourise Tepet Ejava's lower body with Green Sun Nimbus Flare and have it be possible for her to be kept alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real world people can <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_17573_7-fatal-injuries-that-people-somehow-survived.html\" target=\"_blank\">survive being cut in half</a>, so it should certainly be possible for one of the Exalted.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T06:28:35-08:00","id":71943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71901#post71901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just like framing such things in terms of specific narratives, and that one appeals to me because the Roseblack is worthy of a badass green jade lower body prosthetic, and Green Sun Princes have Charms to shoot toxic fire, God knows they <i>should</i> be disintegrating large portions of people's bodies.[/SPOILER]</div> </div> </div> </div>*imagines Roseblack using 3e Resistance Charms to come back from being de-lower-half-a-tated*<br /> <br /> *smiles*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T07:20:34-08:00","id":71961,"title":"","content":"On an unrelated note, I almost replied in the &quot;How Dangerous Should the Wyld Hunt Be?&quot; thread with, &quot;About as dangerous as Vance's cat,&quot; but I felt more like sharing an anecdote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T07:57:12-08:00","id":71975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71943#post71943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*imagines Roseblack using 3e Resistance Charms to come back from being de-lower-half-a-tated*<br /> <br /> *smiles*</div> </div> </div> </div>Goood gooood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T08:22:09-08:00","id":71986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71943#post71943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*imagines Roseblack using 3e Resistance Charms to come back from being de-lower-half-a-tated*<br /> <br /> *smiles*</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like Negezzer should get in on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T11:37:06-08:00","id":72108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71986#post71986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like Negezzer should get in on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>He managed to live through the experience. That's no guarantee of retaining full function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T11:42:18-08:00","id":72112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71986#post71986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like Negezzer should get in on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he doesn't have sufficient Resistance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T18:00:23-08:00","id":72352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71986#post71986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like Negezzer should get in on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No amount of Charm can protect you from feeling human feelings. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Or at least, no amount of Dragon-Blood Charm. There may be weird mindwarping transhumanism effects that make your basic modality of reality non-human in some significant degree)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T18:51:14-08:00","id":72386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71986#post71986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like Negezzer should get in on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said this before, but one thing idea that I'd love to see the fandom drop is this idea that any Exalt can just choose to invest xp where they want and buy whatever Charms they are mechanically viable for. Of course A PLAYER can make those choices, because they are in control of their character's themes and narrartive - but characters have strengths and weaknesses and like people in reality do not have absolute self-control over what those are. <i><b>Except for Alchemicals</b></i>, characters do not actually get a Charm menu they get to order off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T19:12:15-08:00","id":72402,"title":"","content":"To some extent, a character can choose to invest XP where they wish. They might not be aware of the out-of-game mechanics, but I think most PCs grok 'If I want to get better at X, I should find a way to practice or study X.'<br /> <br /> I assume that Dynasts know that you can strengthen your body through by increasing the flow of your chi in your muscles or something. Whether through yoga, martial arts,breathing exercises, or meditating on the element of earth. In the real world, you can learn to be resistant enough to take a hit or walk across burning coals. In Exalted, you can learn to be resistant enough to take a sword hit or walk across burning lava.<br /> <br /> Neither of these happen by accident though. They're both the product of someone going 'I want to be able to X, so I shall do Y.'<br /> <br /> Of course, there are charms you learn whether you want to or not and times when you want to learn things but can't. If a terrestrial exalted who loves music and the arts is imprisoned to do hard labor underground, hes probably going to 'learn' charms that help with hard labor, keeping healthy while eating little food, and navigating in poorly lit areas. Likewise, if he's spending 14 hours a day mining for jade with his bare hands, his desire to get better at studying or preparing delicious meals will probably not be satisfied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-14-2014, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T20:59:55-08:00","id":72449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72402#post72402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To some extent, a character can choose to invest XP where they wish. They might not be aware of the out-of-game mechanics, but I think most PCs grok 'If I want to get better at X, I should find a way to practice or study X.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think glamourweave just annoy at question like &quot;Negezzer's leg is still broken, just learn some Medicine/Resistance charm&quot; or &quot;Denovah still have a missing eye ? Can he just go borrow some Growing Missing Eye Hearthstone ?&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T00:32:25-08:00","id":72500,"title":"","content":"A Bureaucracy esque charm, one that works on a whole magnitude of people to make them live and be healthier.<br /> <br /> Was anything like that brought up already or already exists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T01:24:10-08:00","id":72512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72386#post72386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said this before, but one thing idea that I'd love to see the fandom drop is this idea that any Exalt can just choose to invest xp where they want and buy whatever Charms they are mechanically viable for. Of course A PLAYER can make those choices, because they are in control of their character's themes and narrartive - but characters have strengths and weaknesses and like people in reality do not have absolute self-control over what those are. <i><b>Except for Alchemicals</b></i>, characters do not actually get a Charm menu they get to order off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in his backstory, Negezzar initiated into Celestial Martial Arts and learned the pre-form Wood Dragon Charms in an attempt to heal his leg.<br /> <br /> I suppose you might make an exception for MA Charms and other things that require tutelage, like Sorcery. In any case, I disagree with your interpretation.<br /> <br /> I understand that the 1e idea of learning Charms from manuals is being downplayed, but I find the other extreme of characters not being able to choose how to harness their own Essence to be thoroughly silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T03:39:07-08:00","id":72542,"title":"","content":"More musings:<br /> <br /> I don't know if this is more Abyssal-ish, but reinforcing the basic frame of the subject surgically should be in Medicine. Redundancy in organs. Reinforced bones. Brain moved to the chestular region for safe-keeping. Let people get their Dr. Frankenstein on in a different way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T04:32:00-08:00","id":72546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=70956#post70956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There won't be a Charm to make your nurses just as effective as you</div> </div> </div> </div>Random mortal nurses, no. But I'd like an effect along the lines of something that lets the Solar make Dragon-Blooded disciples (temporarily) as effective at healing as he is, skilled mortal doctors supernaturally effective, and unskilled mortals now as good as trained doctors. Faced with an outbreak of a plague, the Dragon-Blooded should be tempted to strike a deal with the golden glowing Anathema, who can make them (no matter how well-prepared they are in Age of Sorrow terms) far more effective . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T06:18:14-08:00","id":72575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72512#post72512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that the 1e idea of learning Charms from manuals is being downplayed, but I find the other extreme of characters not being able to choose how to harness their own Essence to be thoroughly silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players =/= Characters<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible for an Exalted character to have absolutely no talent in a certain area and to be unable to develop certain charms. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T07:03:54-08:00","id":72602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72575#post72575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Players =/= Characters<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible for an Exalted character to have absolutely no talent in a certain area and to be unable to develop certain charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise to just think it's too hard and not worth the time and effort that they can use on something they feel is more important, like their crippling drug addiction.<br /> One doesn't just tell a drug-addicted (or fae-addicted) solar &quot;Pff, whatever man, man up and learn integrity charms&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T09:24:56-08:00","id":72660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72512#post72512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, in his backstory, Negezzar initiated into Celestial Martial Arts and learned the pre-form Wood Dragon Charms in an attempt to heal his leg.<br /> <br /> I suppose you might make an exception for MA Charms and other things that require tutelage, like Sorcery. In any case, I disagree with your interpretation.<br /> <br /> I understand that the 1e idea of learning Charms from manuals is being downplayed, but I find the other extreme of characters not being able to choose how to harness their own Essence to be thoroughly silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're overstating something that's a bit more like this:<br /> <br /> You can't choose <i>what you're good at</i>. If you really want to and are really dedicated, you can perhaps potentially learn some of it through painful dedication, but it won't be easy and not everyone is up to that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> If you're a swordsman, though, you can totally choose to focus on defense or offense; if you're a doctor, you can choose to focus on learning how to cure certain diseases vs learning how to treat injuries. The point is that Negezzar can't simply choose to be one of the greatest Terrestrial doctors just because it would be useful to him.<br /> <br /> (A PC in that situation could tell the story about how their character, through painful dedication, manages to become a master of medicine anyway, buying all the charms at an unfavored cost etc. But it's not something most people are realistically capable of. It's assumed that PCs can write their character's story to an extent, essentially, especially when it comes to personality, so if you insist that your character can find some hidden reserve of will and learn Medicine despite having no talent -- and are willing to spend unfavored costs and endure long training times -- then they can; but the barrier is meant to be higher, thematically, than just spending a few more XP. The only reason it's relatively low mechanically is because it's better for the game to give you the option to tell stories like that if you want to.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:10:24-08:00","id":72681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72575#post72575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Players =/= Characters<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible for an Exalted character to have absolutely no talent in a certain area and to be unable to develop certain charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely possible for an Exalted character to have no interest in a certain area or not have the time/energy/resources to develop it. <br /> <br /> For almost every human skill, a person becomes good at it through study and practice, not because they have some nebulous 'talent.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:21:51-08:00","id":72684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72681#post72681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For almost every human skill, a person becomes good at it through study and practice, not because they have some nebulous 'talent.'</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be either or both.<br /> <br /> There are people who'll never be good at certain things no matter how hard they try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:09:16-08:00","id":72721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72684#post72684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can be either or both.<br /> <br /> There are people who'll never be good at certain things no matter how hard they try.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't actually believe that unless you're talking about some physical or mental disability. Even then, I've seen people with one arm perform acts that I've struggled to do with two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:16:36-08:00","id":72726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72721#post72721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't actually believe that unless you're talking about some physical or mental disability. Even then, I've seen people with one arm perform acts that I've struggled to do with two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making an exception for &quot;physical or mental disability&quot; actually opens the door wider than I think you probably intended, because &quot;disability&quot; is calibrated relative to the norm. You can't play the theremin well without perfect pitch, but we don't consider that a disability because, well, most people lack perfect pitch and anyhow it's not very relevant to life in our society. If almost everybody had perfect pitch and we designed things under the assumption that users had it, then it would be considered a disability.<br /> <br /> Put another way: in the kingdom of the blind, the one-eyed king would probably not be considered &quot;less disabled&quot;, but rather would be thought of as having an amazing special ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:24:17-08:00","id":72731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=71937#post71937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real world people can <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_17573_7-fatal-injuries-that-people-somehow-survived.html\" target=\"_blank\">survive being cut in half</a>, so it should certainly be possible for one of the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be frank though, most of the obvious causes of surviving the loss of your lower body do not also blast you with uber radiation that threatens to liquify your innards and cover you in lumpy cancerous growths, terminating in total dissolution into a dust where your suffering will last for a ten thousand years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T12:37:06-08:00","id":72771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72726#post72726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making an exception for &quot;physical or mental disability&quot; actually opens the door wider than I think you probably intended, because &quot;disability&quot; is calibrated relative to the norm. You can't play the theremin well without perfect pitch, but we don't consider that a disability because, well, most people lack perfect pitch and anyhow it's not very relevant to life in our society. If almost everybody had perfect pitch and we designed things under the assumption that users had it, then it would be considered a disability.<br /> <br /> Put another way: in the kingdom of the blind, the one-eyed king would probably not be considered &quot;less disabled&quot;, but rather would be thought of as having an amazing special ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, in a society where everyone had perfect pitch, a person who didn't would be considered disabled. That doesn't actually refute my statement that outside of disabilities, people spend time practicing something will likely get better at it.<br /> <br /> Disabled is a cultural construct, but so is the level of skill required for a culture to consider you good at something. If you're going to imagine a world where everyone is blind then a blind person can easily have good or excellent levels of perception because the the metric by which he's judged changes.<br /> <br /> Of course, I haven't seen an Exalted game where the level of dots you have in Attributes and Abilities changes depending on which nation you're in. The question is if there's a Dragon-Blood with archery 0 who can never reach archery 2 (the minimum level required to gain a non-excellency charm) no matter the amount of time and energy she spends training in archery but is otherwise hale and healthy.<br /> <br /> Sure, there might be one, but for 99% of the DB that's not going to be the case because for 99% of mortals, if you can spend a year training with a bow and arrow, you can hit 2 dots in that skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T13:04:40-08:00","id":72785,"title":"","content":"Maybe a charm that would let the Solar shoulder the suffering and injuries of others himself? The Solar could run his hand across someone's wound, and that wound would vanish, and an identical wound would open on the Solar's body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T13:26:34-08:00","id":72798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72771#post72771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, in a society where everyone had perfect pitch, a person who didn't would be considered disabled. That doesn't actually refute my statement that outside of disabilities, people spend time practicing something will likely get better at it.<br /> <br /> Disabled is a cultural construct, but so is the level of skill required for a culture to consider you good at something. If you're going to imagine a world where everyone is blind then a blind person can easily have good or excellent levels of perception because the the metric by which he's judged changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehn, maybe I didn't explain myself very well. What I mean is that, if you're willing to accept that there are innate disabilities can simply close off certain avenues then it follows that there are innate abilities that can open up otherwise inaccessible avenues, because what's considered &quot;disability&quot; and what's considered &quot;lack of a remarkable special talent&quot; is relative. Once you admit the possibility that innate abilities can gate access to categories of activity, it goes in both directions.<br /> <br /> What I mean to say is that the exemption for disabilities is a really, really big exemption with important implications for the entire issue. I don't dispute the notion that people with different starting aptitudes can usually reach comparable skill levels through training.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T15:50:18-08:00","id":72852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72512#post72512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, in his backstory, Negezzar initiated into Celestial Martial Arts and learned the pre-form Wood Dragon Charms in an attempt to heal his leg.<br /> <br /> I suppose you might make an exception for MA Charms and other things that require tutelage, like Sorcery. In any case, I disagree with your interpretation.<br /> <br /> I understand that the 1e idea of learning Charms from manuals is being downplayed, but I find the other extreme of characters not being able to choose how to harness their own Essence to be thoroughly silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Martial Arts styles are a special case of specifically constructed learneable disciplines, not a character's personal epic skills mechanically represented.<br /> <br /> 2) You can choose to make yourself more skilled at something through practice and focus, but that doesn't mean Tesla could have been Mozart if he'd just focused on music instead of science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T15:56:52-08:00","id":72855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72721#post72721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't actually believe that unless you're talking about some physical or mental disability. Even then, I've seen people with one arm perform acts that I've struggled to do with two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone with enough practice and discipline and the basic physical ability might be able to rise from 0 dots in an Ability to 2 dots - sure. But practice and discipline alone can not make someone a Picasso, a Sherlock Holmes, a Tesla, etc. Charms represent epic transcendent abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T15:58:55-08:00","id":72857,"title":"","content":"Apparently an almost sanity breaking childhood of intense one-on-one education can result in a Miles though.<br /> <br /> Or at least speaking three languages and being a published author by ten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T16:11:00-08:00","id":72865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72721#post72721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, I've seen people with one arm perform acts that I've struggled to do with two.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that doesn't suggest that there are people with inherent legs up or different upper thresholds in ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T16:21:53-08:00","id":72871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72865#post72865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that doesn't suggest that there are people with inherent legs up or different upper thresholds in ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it does. And?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T20:08:17-08:00","id":72967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72681#post72681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For almost every human skill, a person becomes good at it through study and practice, not because they have some nebulous 'talent.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Just quoting this to say it's absolutely true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1954-spigot","name":"spigot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1954_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T00:37:09-08:00","id":73076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72681#post72681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't actually believe that unless you're talking about some physical or mental disability. Even then, I've seen people with one arm perform acts that I've struggled to do with two. .'</div> </div> </div> </div>There are 'disabilities' that are both more subtle and much harder to get around then missing a arm. The most common ones tends to be things like poor depth perception, lack of fine motor control or defective sense of balance. All of those prevent you from ever becoming 'good' at something that depends on them, for instance I'll never be able to draw a decent looking circle or write decent looking text without mechanical aid and I've had many many hours of practise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T03:17:22-08:00","id":73120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=73076#post73076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are 'disabilities' that are both more subtle and much harder to get around then missing a arm. The most common ones tends to be things like poor depth perception, lack of fine motor control or defective sense of balance. All of those prevent you from ever becoming 'good' at something that depends on them, for instance I'll never be able to draw a decent looking circle or write decent looking text without mechanical aid and I've had many many hours of practise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know a professional concept artist who wears glasses, she can't draw a decent looking anything without mechanical aid, but most people would still say she's good at drawing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T03:49:54-08:00","id":73123,"title":"","content":"I don't believe &quot;Talent&quot; exists. Talent is merely a skill for which there is no easy way to describe the factors that went into acquiring the skill. There may be many, even dozens of factors for why someone is skilled. What tends to rub people the wrong way about talent, I feel, is that it implies some people are just fated/destined to be better at something than another person is, and that bugs people's sense of egalatarianism. The fact remains that different circumstances can limit or aid someone in subtle ways which might as well be undetectable unless you have an extremely detailed life portrait of a person which would take you almost as much time to analyze as it did for them to live it, so it's all moot anyways.<br /> <br /> All this being said, attempting to model that level of granularity in a game is ridiculous, and &quot;Talent/No Talent&quot; is just as suitable explanation as any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":". 02-16-2014, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T09:44:31-08:00","id":73237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=73120#post73120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know a professional concept artist who wears glasses, she can't draw a decent looking anything without mechanical aid, but most people would still say she's good at drawing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you had to pick one of your acquaintances to draw your summoning circle for you, she wouldn't be at the top of the list right? Personally I like the idea of there being charm equivalents of lack of fine motor control, dyslexia etc. I wouldn't want mechanics for it but I think it's neat to be able to make a character that always wanted to be a martial artist but just couldn't get the forms right and ended up as the family accountant instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T11:34:49-08:00","id":73278,"title":"","content":"How about charms that utilize more long-term effects of medical knowledge for groups/area's? Something that may simulate immunization of populace against specific health hazards.<br /> <br /> Examples: Creating an elixir that in concentrated doses can sure someone of a disease within a few moments; but in small regular doses can provide an effective immunity to that disease?<br /> <br /> Also something that lets a solar who has followers/cult or rules a population make that population stronger over generations by influencing their health? Want your people to be just a little stronger or more agile? With this charm, after three generations your populace will exhibit those kinds of traits.All due to different health programs/taboo's that the charm gives some supernatural oomph to help them take effect faster.<br /> <br /> Medicine/health charms have some great (if a little un-epic feeling) applications in the here and now. But the ability can really stand apart if used over long periods of time on small populations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1027-deamion","name":"Deamion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1027_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T12:47:08-08:00","id":73311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spigot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=72967#post72967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just quoting this to say it's absolutely true.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=73123#post73123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe &quot;Talent&quot; exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>God, Jimi Hendrix must just be a mind-blowing experience for some folks...<br /> <br /> Or Mozart.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T13:34:56-08:00","id":73341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/70267-ex3-solar-medicine?p=73311#post73311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> God, Jimi Hendrix must just be a mind-blowing experience for some folks...<br /> <br /> Or Mozart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you do me a favor and not do things like quote me out of context, considering my initial statement hinges heavily <b>on the entire rest of my post.</b> Don't be cute just to try and make a glib remark. You just end up looking like a jerk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T18:12:08-08:00","id":73994,"title":"","content":"So, something else I'd like from 3e charms in general is more flavor text and/or charms that integrate the flavor directly into the effect. 2e's Solar charms were ..less than good about this in several places. For example:<br /> <br /> Craftsman Needs No Tools (2e)<br /> <br /> The Chosen bring harmony to Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Craftsman Needs No Tools (1e)<br /> <br /> The greatest burden of a craftsman is the pressing need for tools and a workshop. For an Exalted who has mastered this Charm, that is no problem at all. A character who knows this Charm can work directly with her chosen material, shaping it with hands and voice, laboring without any need for tools. Characters using this Charm slowly croon and purr to their work as they shape and form the material with their fingertips \u2014 the effect is the same as working in a well-stocked workshop, and in many cases, better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T18:17:12-08:00","id":74000,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the 2e thing where every charm opened with a tangential aphorism about the splat kind of annoyed me. It was cute here and there but it faded into a drone after a while, like I was listening to Solar Party Propaganda missives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T04:24:10-08:00","id":76182,"title":"","content":"So I saw the Lazarus Part of the thread and a thought occurred to me. When Jesus raised Lazarus from the dead, he was subverting the powers of death. In fact, Christians believe that's what Christ did: He made forgiveness of people's faults easily available to the masses thus saving them from their spiritual &quot;death&quot;. In the real world, physical death is an event. Spiritual death is a condition (according to religious texts at least). But in Exalted, death is an actual tangible thing. It is a source of power. It is an overlord and it's minions are physical sword wielding antagonists. So if you're looking at making a Solar Medicine charm based on Jesus, I would suggest having a series of charms designed to subvert the power of death over the masses. This can involve curing the effects of living in shadow lands, destroying necrotech (or whatever it will be called in 3e), and possibly using your own 'death' to release the masses from the power of a deathlord.<br /> <br /> Here's what I think this charm tree would look like:<br /> <br /> 1) &quot;Trust me. I'm a doctor.&quot; (Mentioned in previous posts. Doesn't have to be an automatic success instead gives a small bonus by helping you look the part of the doctor, even if you are a quack). Essence 1<br /> 2) &quot;Hold on! The doctor's on his way!&quot; (Mentioned in previous posts). Essence 2-3.<br /> 3) &quot;You're nothing but a bag of bones!&quot; (Damages Necrotic creations). Essence 2-3.<br /> 4) &quot;You're better now, but maybe you should consider moving.&quot; (Cures effects of living in shadowlands for long periods of time). Essence 2-3?<br /> 5) &quot;I will heal your lands!&quot; (Evokes small benefits to large groups. Nothing along the lines of &quot;cure the contagion&quot;, but making people more healthy. Death of the solar results in widespread cure of ailments and protection for lands with a positive intimacy towards the solar). Essence 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":2346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","user":"Demac","date":". 02-21-2014, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T09:57:46-08:00","id":76359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often use the metaphor of spiritual radiation poisoning to describe shadowlands. I fully endorse medicine charms to ameliorate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Changing an area's status relative to parallel realities seems like a Sorcery thing to me (or maybe a Sidereal/Infernal Charm, since they get reality-warping effects much like Sorcery). Then again, I do not find it any more questionable than Wyld-Cauldron, which people seem to find indisputably Solar for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T16:01:42-08:00","id":76669,"title":"","content":"There is nothing that says that Sorcery can't do the same things as Charms do.<br /> <br /> Well, outside of the to be expected infringement on unique niches, but frankly, having Sorcery Spells as the <i>relatively</i> easy to access but expensive to use and circumstantially useful powers versus the more flexible, cheaper and potentially more powerful Charms could be an interesting way to handle the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/705-hazard","name":"Hazard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}